1
00:00:00,375 --> 00:00:01,416
(Sound of a wall clock pendulum)

2
00:00:01,541 --> 00:00:03,125
World War II,

3
00:00:03,208 --> 00:00:05,208
Iran had declared itself neutral.

4
00:00:05,791 --> 00:00:07,125
But when the war,

5
00:00:07,166 --> 00:00:09,541
reached its peak intensity on the Russian front,

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,041
this neutrality became shaky!

7
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:16,125
On the night of the second of Shahrivar 1320,

8
00:00:16,458 --> 00:00:17,458
that is, at a time when,

9
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,583
the rumor of the Allies attacking Iran,

10
00:00:19,625 --> 00:00:21,291
to help the Russian army,

11
00:00:21,583 --> 00:00:23,208
had terrified everyone,

12
00:00:23,625 --> 00:00:24,416
Uncle Colonel,

13
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:27,916
on the occasion of the reconciliation between Aqa Jan and Uncle Napoleon,

14
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:30,375
invited the whole family to dinner.

15
00:00:31,291 --> 00:00:33,416
After a long time away from Lily,

16
00:00:33,458 --> 00:00:34,875
my heart was happy to see her!

17
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:39,166
But the suspicion I had about Aqa Jan's hidden intentions

18
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:41,500
worried me greatly!

19
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:43,375
The only person who could

20
00:00:43,375 --> 00:00:45,583
prevent a possible disaster

21
00:00:45,583 --> 00:00:47,250
was Prince Asdollah Mirza,

22
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:49,708
a high-ranking member of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs,

23
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:52,333
who had also made himself comfortable in Shir-Ali the butcher's house,

24
00:00:52,375 --> 00:00:53,541
and getting him out seemed impossible!

25
00:00:53,916 --> 00:00:56,208
(End of narration)

26
00:00:57,125 --> 00:01:01,750
Uncle Napoleon Episode 7

27
00:01:03,083 --> 00:01:07,916
Based on the novel "Dear Uncle Napoleon" by Iraj Pezeshkzad

28
00:01:08,791 --> 00:01:10,791
Subtitles: Iman Soleimani Zadeh

29
00:01:14,083 --> 00:01:16,083
(Sound of horses running and riders' clamor)

30
00:02:07,541 --> 00:02:10,750
♪ Ride of the valkyrie ♪

31
00:02:55,625 --> 00:02:56,541
Roll already, roll!

32
00:02:56,666 --> 00:02:57,583
This hand's a gammon!

33
00:02:57,625 --> 00:02:58,708
Four and two.

34
00:02:59,208 --> 00:03:00,833
You don't need to guide me.

35
00:03:00,875 --> 00:03:02,000
Obviously I'm closing it!

36
00:03:02,250 --> 00:03:03,166
This four...

37
00:03:03,291 --> 00:03:04,000
And this two!

38
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:06,750
Now if you can... - It's true you defeated the British, I admit!

39
00:03:06,916 --> 00:03:07,625
But that,

40
00:03:07,666 --> 00:03:09,083
was on the battlefield.

41
00:03:09,250 --> 00:03:09,958
But in backgammon,

42
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,791
believe me, you don't know how to play.

43
00:03:11,916 --> 00:03:13,166
If I were you,

44
00:03:13,208 --> 00:03:14,541
I wouldn't play backgammon anymore. - Roll, Aqa Jan!

45
00:03:14,708 --> 00:03:16,541
The night is young!

46
00:03:16,541 --> 00:03:17,291
Roll!

47
00:03:17,416 --> 00:03:18,208
Double four.

48
00:03:18,375 --> 00:03:20,208
Hit and closed!

49
00:03:20,250 --> 00:03:21,083
This isn't a game,

50
00:03:21,333 --> 00:03:22,416
it's luck!

51
00:03:23,166 --> 00:03:24,666
Sit and watch.

52
00:03:24,708 --> 00:03:25,916
With your permission.

53
00:03:26,291 --> 00:03:27,541
Five and six.

54
00:03:27,750 --> 00:03:29,833
It's not right for you to just sit there

55
00:03:29,833 --> 00:03:30,916
while I keep rolling the dice!

56
00:03:31,083 --> 00:03:31,958
It just isn't!

57
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,125
Lily dear...

58
00:03:33,125 --> 00:03:34,541
Go get a book or a newspaper

59
00:03:34,583 --> 00:03:35,250
for Dad to read!

60
00:03:35,291 --> 00:03:35,875
I'll go get it!

61
00:03:36,291 --> 00:03:36,583
Lily!

62
00:03:36,583 --> 00:03:37,875
All the houses are closed.

63
00:03:38,166 --> 00:03:40,000
What will you do with this hit piece?

64
00:03:40,583 --> 00:03:42,000
Spare me the poetry,

65
00:03:42,041 --> 00:03:43,416
or I'll send for the Shahnameh.

66
00:03:43,625 --> 00:03:45,166
It's not over till it's over,

67
00:03:45,208 --> 00:03:46,250
♪ Traditional music ♪

68
00:03:46,250 --> 00:03:49,416
Lord, never let a beggar rise in the world, - Put on another record.-

69
00:03:49,416 --> 00:03:52,833
For once he rises, he forgets God!

70
00:03:52,833 --> 00:03:54,416
Knock on wood,

71
00:03:54,458 --> 00:03:55,333
So far they're good!

72
00:03:55,375 --> 00:03:56,916
(Laughter and crowd murmur)

73
00:03:56,958 --> 00:03:57,833
Lily dear...

74
00:03:58,333 --> 00:03:59,708
Play a ninash-nash jig...

75
00:03:59,750 --> 00:04:00,083
Yes!

76
00:04:00,708 --> 00:04:01,750
Please, go ahead.

77
00:04:01,750 --> 00:04:02,791
Thank you.

78
00:04:02,958 --> 00:04:04,833
♪ Background music by Master Javad Badizadeh titled "Kheili Ghashange" ♪

79
00:04:04,833 --> 00:04:06,958
It seems you haven't drunk any of this wine yet.

80
00:04:07,875 --> 00:04:08,666
Take a sip!

81
00:04:09,625 --> 00:04:10,208
Colonel,

82
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,416
Any news from Asdollah?

83
00:04:12,708 --> 00:04:13,375
No news?

84
00:04:13,416 --> 00:04:14,166
Oh! Let it go, man!

85
00:04:14,166 --> 00:04:16,333
You still haven't let go of this Asdollah?

86
00:04:16,375 --> 00:04:17,041
- Cheers.

87
00:04:17,041 --> 00:04:18,916
In your opinion, what kind of wine is this, Doctor?

88
00:04:18,958 --> 00:04:20,125
With Dustali around, you can't even tell

89
00:04:20,166 --> 00:04:21,458
what poison you're drinking!

90
00:04:21,541 --> 00:04:25,208
(Sound of music and crowd murmur)

91
00:04:26,583 --> 00:04:27,208
Well!

92
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:28,500
Well, what happened? What happened?

93
00:04:30,083 --> 00:04:30,625
You, Sir,

94
00:04:30,625 --> 00:04:33,000
make us do such shameful things!

95
00:04:33,375 --> 00:04:35,000
We weren't speaking to this baker,

96
00:04:35,041 --> 00:04:36,875
but for you we went to see him!

97
00:04:37,416 --> 00:04:38,625
And after he took the money,

98
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:40,291
he played hard to get for a whole hour,

99
00:04:40,291 --> 00:04:41,625
till he finally agreed.

100
00:04:41,833 --> 00:04:43,125
We went to the police station together,

101
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:45,125
and there the baker dropped the charges.

102
00:04:45,583 --> 00:04:46,375
Well done!

103
00:04:46,416 --> 00:04:47,791
I'll drink to your health...

104
00:04:49,625 --> 00:04:51,791
So Shir-Ali will be released!

105
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:53,500
And tonight he'll go home. Right?

106
00:04:53,541 --> 00:04:54,916
No, Sir! Why lie?

107
00:04:54,958 --> 00:04:56,875
The grave is this close!

108
00:04:57,541 --> 00:04:58,916
They said the chief isn't there.

109
00:04:58,958 --> 00:05:01,291
Until the chief comes, he won't be released.

110
00:05:01,291 --> 00:05:02,750
S... s... so when is this chief coming!

111
00:05:03,625 --> 00:05:04,791
They said he's gone till tomorrow.

112
00:05:05,041 --> 00:05:06,750
He might drop by tonight too.

113
00:05:06,958 --> 00:05:08,375
I paid all this money

114
00:05:08,416 --> 00:05:10,291
so they release him tomorrow?

115
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:11,958
So this good-for-nothing

116
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,750
is sleeping there tonight too, huh?

117
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:14,958
Serves him right!

118
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,750
Shouldn't have drawn a cleaver on people!

119
00:05:16,958 --> 00:05:19,333
I'm not talking about Shir-Ali!

120
00:05:19,625 --> 00:05:19,958
Then who?

121
00:05:19,958 --> 00:05:21,000
Where is your common sense!

122
00:05:21,166 --> 00:05:25,833
Just us and four old Hassan Moosi muskets...

123
00:05:26,083 --> 00:05:28,416
The men had no equipment.

124
00:05:28,791 --> 00:05:30,458
They were hungry.

125
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:33,083
Their rations and pay never arrived on time.

126
00:05:33,291 --> 00:05:36,083
But Khodadad Khan the rebel was not alone!

127
00:05:36,291 --> 00:05:38,291
A great empire

128
00:05:38,333 --> 00:05:39,708
was behind him!

129
00:05:39,875 --> 00:05:42,583
If we had even two or three good rifles,

130
00:05:42,625 --> 00:05:44,833
we'd seized them as spoils!

131
00:05:44,916 --> 00:05:46,750
We'd kept one for ourselves,

132
00:05:46,791 --> 00:05:49,291
and given one or two to our men!

133
00:05:49,375 --> 00:05:51,125
And one you gave me to carry on my shoulder!

134
00:05:51,250 --> 00:05:53,750
Yes, I had given one to Ghasem too!

135
00:05:53,791 --> 00:05:56,583
Not because he was a good shooter...

136
00:05:56,625 --> 00:05:59,000
But because he was my orderly,

137
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,833
and his duty was to protect me.

138
00:06:01,958 --> 00:06:03,416
Believe me,

139
00:06:03,666 --> 00:06:05,583
even then the British

140
00:06:05,791 --> 00:06:08,791
plotted against me several times,

141
00:06:09,041 --> 00:06:09,750
you know?

142
00:06:09,791 --> 00:06:12,125
Because of killing that traitor...

143
00:06:12,166 --> 00:06:13,500
Khodadad Khan the rebel!

144
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:15,708
If Sir hadn't killed that shameless wretch,

145
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:18,166
what chaos would have broken out in this region!

146
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,416
You never did tell us

147
00:06:20,458 --> 00:06:23,000
how you managed to kill Khodadad Khan.

148
00:06:23,708 --> 00:06:25,708
God was on our side!

149
00:06:25,875 --> 00:06:27,666
Because the distance between us

150
00:06:27,708 --> 00:06:30,000
was more than 100 paces!

151
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:31,458
I,

152
00:06:31,458 --> 00:06:32,416
took aim right at the middle

153
00:06:32,458 --> 00:06:34,625
of his throat!

154
00:06:34,625 --> 00:06:36,291
No, no, Sir, it wasn't his throat!

155
00:06:36,333 --> 00:06:38,291
It was right between his eyebrows!

156
00:06:38,375 --> 00:06:38,791
Ah...

157
00:06:38,833 --> 00:06:40,583
What an ass you are, Ghasem!

158
00:06:40,583 --> 00:06:41,916
You won't let me speak!

159
00:06:41,958 --> 00:06:43,541
That's what I meant.

160
00:06:43,583 --> 00:06:46,291
You see, my rifle shot a little high...

161
00:06:46,458 --> 00:06:49,708
So I deliberately aimed at the middle of his throat,

162
00:06:49,750 --> 00:06:52,375
so it would hit right between his eyebrows.

163
00:06:52,458 --> 00:06:54,250
Looks like Sir is right!

164
00:06:54,375 --> 00:06:58,083
I called on Imam Ali...

165
00:06:58,333 --> 00:06:59,625
and pulled the trigger.

166
00:06:59,625 --> 00:07:00,500
Baaaaaaaang!

167
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:01,958
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

168
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,041
- God help us, God help us!

169
00:07:04,083 --> 00:07:06,875
Sir! When the bullet hit right between his eyebrows,

170
00:07:06,916 --> 00:07:08,416
he let out a groan

171
00:07:08,458 --> 00:07:10,416
that shook the entire mountain and desert!

172
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:12,791
I realized the shot had hit its target.

173
00:07:13,958 --> 00:07:17,000
Sir, all hell broke loose!

174
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:20,333
Each of them started running in different directions!

175
00:07:20,791 --> 00:07:23,041
But we didn't let them get away!

176
00:07:23,375 --> 00:07:24,625
We chased after them.

177
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:25,833
We took about...

178
00:07:25,875 --> 00:07:28,708
thirty or forty prisoners from them!

179
00:07:28,708 --> 00:07:29,208
What!

180
00:07:29,458 --> 00:07:30,666
Thirty or forty people?

181
00:07:31,041 --> 00:07:32,125
Come now, Sir!

182
00:07:32,166 --> 00:07:34,666
You've fought so many wars, you've forgotten!

183
00:07:34,916 --> 00:07:36,083
We counted them ourselves.

184
00:07:36,166 --> 00:07:38,125
One, two, three, four...

185
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:39,666
Five, six... - Mash Ghasem... Mash Ghasem

186
00:07:39,666 --> 00:07:40,291
Seven... - Come here

187
00:07:40,375 --> 00:07:41,375
Eight...

188
00:07:41,583 --> 00:07:44,000
In short, only ten of the three hundred were remaned!

189
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,875
Khodadad Khan's brother was among them too.

190
00:07:46,291 --> 00:07:47,708
Do you think

191
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:49,708
the British, who,

192
00:07:49,791 --> 00:07:52,083
to prop up Khodadad Khan the rebel,

193
00:07:52,083 --> 00:07:54,000
spent all that money...

194
00:07:54,041 --> 00:07:55,416
and gave them weapons...

195
00:07:55,458 --> 00:07:56,916
just forgot about it?

196
00:07:56,958 --> 00:07:57,583
Not at all!

197
00:07:57,583 --> 00:07:58,750
After a year,

198
00:07:58,791 --> 00:08:01,208
one of our rifles went missing,

199
00:08:01,250 --> 00:08:03,000
they put together a dossier against me,

200
00:08:03,041 --> 00:08:05,750
and they nearly ruined me completely!

201
00:08:05,750 --> 00:08:06,750
They wanted to destroy me!

202
00:08:06,750 --> 00:08:07,583
Well, well!

203
00:08:07,833 --> 00:08:10,750
So that dossier was about the lost rifle! Right?

204
00:08:10,750 --> 00:08:11,208
Yes!

205
00:08:11,250 --> 00:08:14,125
(Guests' murmur and chatter)

206
00:08:16,125 --> 00:08:17,541
Honestly Sir, why lie!

207
00:08:17,541 --> 00:08:19,583
We don't go into people's houses.

208
00:08:19,625 --> 00:08:20,958
You weren't a coward, Mash Ghasem!

209
00:08:20,958 --> 00:08:22,000
Saeed, where are you going?

210
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,083
I'm fed up with this spluttering Puri.

211
00:08:25,291 --> 00:08:27,500
Honestly I heard they were always watching you!

212
00:08:27,541 --> 00:08:28,208
Yes!

213
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:30,750
They always tried to bother me!

214
00:08:30,791 --> 00:08:32,000
To frame me!

215
00:08:32,250 --> 00:08:33,875
You weren't a coward, Mash Ghasem dear.

216
00:08:33,916 --> 00:08:35,291
Honestly Sir, why lie!

217
00:08:35,333 --> 00:08:36,875
This Shir-Ali...

218
00:08:36,916 --> 00:08:38,541
has us scared stiff.

219
00:08:39,208 --> 00:08:40,833
Shir-Ali is not at home.

220
00:08:40,833 --> 00:08:41,708
He's in prison.

221
00:08:41,708 --> 00:08:42,958
I'll come with you myself

222
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:43,791
as far as the alley door! - No, Sir!

223
00:08:43,791 --> 00:08:45,708
We will come with you up to the alley door,

224
00:08:45,750 --> 00:08:46,916
The rest is up to you.

225
00:08:47,083 --> 00:08:49,166
You must talk to Asdollah!

226
00:08:49,416 --> 00:08:51,166
He doesn't believe my words!

227
00:08:51,833 --> 00:08:54,125
Mash Ghasem, I'll give you anything you want.

228
00:08:54,125 --> 00:08:54,708
Do you want money?

229
00:08:54,916 --> 00:08:55,375
Huh?

230
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:57,666
How much... how much do you want? - Sir, you stay behind the wall

231
00:08:57,916 --> 00:08:59,583
and cover us.

232
00:08:59,666 --> 00:09:01,500
We go in front, you follow behind.

233
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:02,000
Very good, okay!

234
00:09:02,041 --> 00:09:03,333
Whatever you say! Go, go! - Very good, let's go.

235
00:09:12,750 --> 00:09:14,083
Curse him.

236
00:09:14,083 --> 00:09:15,625
Curse that Dustali

237
00:09:15,666 --> 00:09:16,958
for driving the boy away.

238
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,458
No, madam!

239
00:09:18,458 --> 00:09:21,458
That wretch has gone to nurse Shir-Ali's wife!

240
00:09:22,041 --> 00:09:24,291
Ugh, that ugly hag?

241
00:09:24,791 --> 00:09:27,500
During the chaos of the Constitutional Revolution,

242
00:09:27,583 --> 00:09:30,291
despite all my sacrifices,

243
00:09:30,416 --> 00:09:32,666
they wanted to ruin my reputation.

244
00:09:32,875 --> 00:09:35,291
They wanted to drag me through the mud.

245
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:37,083
They spread rumors everywhere,

246
00:09:37,583 --> 00:09:40,208
In the newspapers of that time they wrote

247
00:09:40,416 --> 00:09:41,208
that I,

248
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:43,833
in the matter of bombarding the parliament,

249
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:45,625
had cooperated with Colonel Liakhov!

250
00:09:45,791 --> 00:09:47,666
It's true!

251
00:09:47,875 --> 00:09:48,958
I was part of the Cossack Brigade,

252
00:09:49,041 --> 00:09:51,333
but,

253
00:09:51,625 --> 00:09:52,166
I swear on the Great Sir's soul,

254
00:09:52,208 --> 00:09:54,833
not even one bullet was fired from my rifle!

255
00:09:54,916 --> 00:09:59,041
Why look far?

256
00:09:59,458 --> 00:10:01,416
You can ask Ghasem.

257
00:10:01,625 --> 00:10:03,708
You can ask him right now.

258
00:10:03,833 --> 00:10:04,791
Ask him,

259
00:10:04,791 --> 00:10:06,833
what I told Shapshal Khan!

260
00:10:06,833 --> 00:10:08,000
Saeed, where is Ghasem?

261
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,666
Uncle, Mash Ghasem had some work and went out.

262
00:10:09,875 --> 00:10:11,083
Hey....

263
00:10:11,125 --> 00:10:14,333
I said some things to Shapshal Khan,

264
00:10:14,375 --> 00:10:15,916
that he very nearly

265
00:10:15,916 --> 00:10:17,750
melted with shame

266
00:10:17,833 --> 00:10:20,000
and sank into the ground!

267
00:10:20,333 --> 00:10:23,708
This... Shapshal Khan, who was he, uncle?

268
00:10:24,125 --> 00:10:26,208
What's your degree for, you jackass?

269
00:10:26,458 --> 00:10:28,083
How do you not know Shapshal Khan!

270
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:28,750
Ah!

271
00:10:29,291 --> 00:10:30,166
This Shapshal Khan,

272
00:10:30,208 --> 00:10:32,125
may God curse him,

273
00:10:32,208 --> 00:10:35,666
was the Russian tutor of Mohammad Ali Shah.

274
00:10:35,958 --> 00:10:37,250
In this city,

275
00:10:37,250 --> 00:10:38,500
there was no one

276
00:10:38,583 --> 00:10:40,625
who was as opposed to the Constitutional Revolution

277
00:10:40,750 --> 00:10:43,458
as Shapshal Khan!

278
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:44,583
They've written this in history too!

279
00:10:47,250 --> 00:10:48,083
My dear Aziz!

280
00:10:48,083 --> 00:10:50,041
Is it true they took Uncle Asdollah to prison?

281
00:10:50,041 --> 00:10:50,708
No, my dear!

282
00:10:50,750 --> 00:10:51,666
They didn't take him to prison.

283
00:10:51,666 --> 00:10:54,041
A shameless woman has imprisoned him!

284
00:10:54,041 --> 00:10:55,208
Oh no! Good heavens!

285
00:10:55,458 --> 00:10:57,041
I wish they would release him soon!

286
00:10:57,083 --> 00:10:58,750
He wanted to take me on a trip.

287
00:10:58,750 --> 00:11:00,000
Take you on a trip?

288
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:00,583
Yes!

289
00:11:00,625 --> 00:11:01,833
Tonight at the party he told me,

290
00:11:01,875 --> 00:11:02,833
if you're a good girl,

291
00:11:02,875 --> 00:11:04,458
I'll take you on a trip to San Francisco!

292
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:06,500
(Everyone laughs)

293
00:11:07,583 --> 00:11:10,000
Damn Asdollah and the things he says.

294
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,666
No... don't curse him!

295
00:11:11,708 --> 00:11:13,916
The poor guy was just joking.

296
00:11:13,958 --> 00:11:15,125
Can you believe it!

297
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,708
On the evening of the same day that,

298
00:11:17,791 --> 00:11:19,208
Malek al-Motakallemin and...

299
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:20,625
Mirza Jahangir Khan and...

300
00:11:20,666 --> 00:11:24,166
a few other Constitutionalists were taken to Bagh-e Shah,

301
00:11:24,708 --> 00:11:27,416
Mohammad Ali Shah summoned Colonel Liakhov,

302
00:11:27,791 --> 00:11:30,583
the commander of the Cossack Brigade,

303
00:11:30,625 --> 00:11:32,041
to congratulate them.

304
00:11:32,541 --> 00:11:35,250
As he was passing in front of our line,

305
00:11:35,291 --> 00:11:36,625
I shouted,

306
00:11:36,666 --> 00:11:37,666
Your Majesty!

307
00:11:37,708 --> 00:11:39,875
You are making a mistake!

308
00:11:39,875 --> 00:11:41,625
These are Constitutionalists!

309
00:11:41,916 --> 00:11:43,916
These are patriots!

310
00:11:43,958 --> 00:11:44,958
They're innocent!

311
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,458
Don't spill their blood!

312
00:11:48,916 --> 00:11:51,416
Mohammad Ali Shah suddenly stopped.

313
00:11:52,250 --> 00:11:53,208
He frowned!

314
00:11:55,041 --> 00:11:58,833
He quietly asked Mohammad Khan Amir al-Omara,

315
00:11:59,416 --> 00:12:01,125
his court minister,

316
00:12:01,666 --> 00:12:03,583
"Who is this?"

317
00:12:04,750 --> 00:12:06,833
When they told him,

318
00:12:06,875 --> 00:12:10,000
"This is so-and-so, son of so-and-so!"

319
00:12:10,250 --> 00:12:12,291
This is the man

320
00:12:12,625 --> 00:12:14,625
who brought peace to the south

321
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:17,583
through his sacrifices...

322
00:12:18,166 --> 00:12:19,541
On your life!

323
00:12:19,708 --> 00:12:21,708
I swear on the Great Sir's soul,

324
00:12:21,750 --> 00:12:24,875
his face turned black as a mulberry!

325
00:12:25,875 --> 00:12:26,916
He said nothing.

326
00:12:27,541 --> 00:12:28,000
He left.

327
00:12:29,083 --> 00:12:29,875
But,

328
00:12:29,875 --> 00:12:30,958
the next day,

329
00:12:30,958 --> 00:12:33,916
my transfer order to Mashhad was issued.

330
00:12:34,875 --> 00:12:36,541
If you don't believe it,

331
00:12:36,791 --> 00:12:38,166
you can ask!

332
00:12:38,333 --> 00:12:40,500
I wasn't alone!

333
00:12:41,250 --> 00:12:45,875
God rest his soul, the late Vali Khan was there.

334
00:12:46,291 --> 00:12:51,208
God rest his soul, the late Alireza Khan Azod al-Molk was there

335
00:12:51,958 --> 00:12:56,625
The late Ali-Qoli Khan Sardar As'ad was there.

336
00:12:58,166 --> 00:13:00,500
When I said this to the Shah,

337
00:13:01,458 --> 00:13:04,500
Shapshal's knees started shaking!

338
00:13:04,916 --> 00:13:07,541
As God is my witness, his whole body

339
00:13:07,625 --> 00:13:09,333
was shaking like a leaf!

340
00:13:10,041 --> 00:13:14,250
But he didn't dare say a word to me!

341
00:13:15,375 --> 00:13:18,208
He started cursing Ghasem!

342
00:13:19,333 --> 00:13:20,750
Isn't that right, Ghasem?

343
00:13:22,375 --> 00:13:22,791
Uncle,

344
00:13:22,833 --> 00:13:24,375
Mash Ghasem hasn't come back yet.

345
00:13:24,833 --> 00:13:27,000
Where has that damn man gone?

346
00:13:27,166 --> 00:13:29,833
And with all these services and sacrifices,

347
00:13:30,041 --> 00:13:32,375
they spread rumors at every gathering,

348
00:13:32,375 --> 00:13:33,125
that so-and-so,

349
00:13:33,291 --> 00:13:34,833
under Colonel Liakhov,

350
00:13:34,875 --> 00:13:36,208
bombarded the parliament!

351
00:13:37,041 --> 00:13:39,791
Whose work do you think these rumors are?

352
00:13:40,083 --> 00:13:40,708
Yes?

353
00:13:41,416 --> 00:13:43,125
It's none other than the British!

354
00:13:43,833 --> 00:13:46,458
Well, they want to take revenge for their defeats,

355
00:13:46,583 --> 00:13:48,833
by ruining my name!

356
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,666
How do we know they won't make me disappear?

357
00:13:52,666 --> 00:13:54,041
With all this war news

358
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:57,208
in the newspapers and on the radio every day,

359
00:13:57,708 --> 00:13:58,166
Well...

360
00:13:58,166 --> 00:14:01,541
They will definitely invade Iran again.

361
00:14:02,125 --> 00:14:05,375
And I'm no longer in a position to stop them.

362
00:14:05,791 --> 00:14:07,291
Moment! Moment!

363
00:14:07,291 --> 00:14:09,208
Tonight the British still haven't shown up, (Crowd murmur and happiness)

364
00:14:09,208 --> 00:14:10,500
Leave them to Hitler.

365
00:14:10,875 --> 00:14:12,000
What happened to my brother?

366
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:13,708
Where is Shamsali?

367
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:14,500
Brother?

368
00:14:14,541 --> 00:14:15,250
What happened?

369
00:14:15,833 --> 00:14:16,750
Asdollah!

370
00:14:16,791 --> 00:14:18,125
So why did they come and tell me

371
00:14:18,125 --> 00:14:19,625
that you were ill!

372
00:14:19,833 --> 00:14:22,500
I've never felt so merry!

373
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:23,625
So this bastard Mash Ghasem,

374
00:14:23,625 --> 00:14:26,125
came and lied to get me here!

375
00:14:26,166 --> 00:14:26,750
Huh?

376
00:14:27,833 --> 00:14:29,708
♪ We came... oh we came... ♪

377
00:14:29,750 --> 00:14:32,875
♪ With music and tambourine we came... ♪ - Oh, you and your antics!

378
00:14:33,250 --> 00:14:34,666
How did you tear yourself away? Huh? Moment!

379
00:14:34,666 --> 00:14:35,375
Moment!

380
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:36,666
We came just to say hello and...

381
00:14:36,666 --> 00:14:37,541
go back!

382
00:14:37,583 --> 00:14:40,375
Wait! Where are you going? Are you going back to that butcher's house again?

383
00:14:40,541 --> 00:14:43,125
Poor woman, her husband is in prison!

384
00:14:43,166 --> 00:14:44,458
She's all alone.

385
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:46,375
Why are these people so heartless!

386
00:14:46,416 --> 00:14:47,291
Ah!

387
00:14:48,833 --> 00:14:50,375
That's lechery, Asdollah style!

388
00:14:50,375 --> 00:14:52,583
Even in lechery, a man should have some finesse!

389
00:14:52,625 --> 00:14:53,500
You said it...

390
00:14:53,541 --> 00:14:54,583
It's wonderful!

391
00:14:55,458 --> 00:14:57,666
It seems tonight is the night of reconciliation! - I just love his antics!

392
00:15:00,458 --> 00:15:02,250
♪ Royal wedding ♪

393
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:04,083
♪ May it be blessed ♪

394
00:15:04,208 --> 00:15:06,041
♪ Great pleasure ♪ - Wow...

395
00:15:06,250 --> 00:15:07,833
♪ May it be blessed ♪ - Help!

396
00:15:08,458 --> 00:15:09,833
Help them!

397
00:15:09,833 --> 00:15:10,458
What happened?

398
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:12,166
What happened Ghasem? What's wrong with you?!

399
00:15:12,208 --> 00:15:13,125
They killed Mr. Dustali Khan!

400
00:15:13,583 --> 00:15:15,958
What happened! Speak up, what happened?!

401
00:15:15,958 --> 00:15:16,958
What happened Mash Ghasem? What's the matter?

402
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,708
Mr. Colonel... What happened to Mr. Dustali Khan?-

403
00:15:18,708 --> 00:15:20,125
Shir-Ali killed Mr. Dustali Khan!

404
00:15:20,166 --> 00:15:22,041
Shameless coward! For God's sake let him go!

405
00:15:22,083 --> 00:15:24,208
You go hide in the house like a woman?

406
00:15:24,208 --> 00:15:25,916
Shir-Ali, the devil misled him, let him go!

407
00:15:25,916 --> 00:15:26,833
Spit it out already!

408
00:15:26,833 --> 00:15:28,875
Mr. Dustali Khan went to Mr. Shir-Ali's house...

409
00:15:28,916 --> 00:15:31,166
It seems he kissed Mrs. Shir-Ali!

410
00:15:31,250 --> 00:15:33,375
Mr. Shir-Ali taught him a lesson.

411
00:15:33,416 --> 00:15:34,500
- Oh... Shir-Ali...

412
00:15:34,541 --> 00:15:36,666
Isn't Shir-Ali in prison?

413
00:15:36,750 --> 00:15:37,791
Shir-Ali was in prison until evening!

414
00:15:37,833 --> 00:15:39,125
The baker went and dropped the charges,

415
00:15:39,166 --> 00:15:40,875
Mr. Shir-Ali was released from prison.

416
00:15:40,958 --> 00:15:43,416
(Crowd murmur)

417
00:15:43,458 --> 00:15:44,916
He's playing with his life...

418
00:15:44,916 --> 00:15:46,083
Come see!

419
00:15:46,666 --> 00:15:47,916
Mr. Dustali Khan!

420
00:15:47,916 --> 00:15:49,250
Mr. Dustali Khan! - Open the door, you coward!

421
00:15:49,250 --> 00:15:50,833
Mr. Dustali Khan!

422
00:15:51,125 --> 00:15:52,333
Mr. Dustali Khan! (Shir-Ali's roars are heard)

423
00:15:52,375 --> 00:15:53,666
Dad... Dad! (Shir-Ali's roars are heard)

424
00:15:53,708 --> 00:15:54,333
Daddy!

425
00:15:54,375 --> 00:15:57,041
Mr. Dustali Khan ran away from Mr. Shir-Ali. - Daddy... There he is! There he is!

426
00:15:57,083 --> 00:15:59,250
He threw himself over the wall into the garden! - Dustali! Dustali!

427
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:00,791
We also closed the alley door! - Dustali, what happened? Speak!

428
00:16:00,833 --> 00:16:01,541
Dustali!

429
00:16:01,583 --> 00:16:02,291
Is he still alive?

430
00:16:02,666 --> 00:16:04,166
Is he still alive? - Oh my God!

431
00:16:04,208 --> 00:16:05,083
Come do something!

432
00:16:05,125 --> 00:16:06,208
Woe is me!

433
00:16:06,708 --> 00:16:08,625
This big bear is behind the door!

434
00:16:08,666 --> 00:16:10,875
You coward, come out!

435
00:16:10,875 --> 00:16:12,291
For God's sake enough! He made a mistake!

436
00:16:12,333 --> 00:16:14,166
He's about to break the door down!

437
00:16:14,208 --> 00:16:15,750
Call the police!

438
00:16:15,791 --> 00:16:17,541
He wants to kill me!

439
00:16:17,541 --> 00:16:19,333
(Crowd murmur)

440
00:16:19,375 --> 00:16:21,333
Help me!

441
00:16:21,333 --> 00:16:23,083
Why are you talking nonsense, Dustali!

442
00:16:23,375 --> 00:16:26,708
Should we call the police and say you sneaked into someone's house!

443
00:16:26,750 --> 00:16:28,791
You went after someone else's wife!

444
00:16:28,791 --> 00:16:31,583
For God's sake go call the police! - Do something!

445
00:16:31,666 --> 00:16:33,041
He's breaking the door down!

446
00:16:33,041 --> 00:16:34,333
He has a cleaver in his hand!

447
00:16:34,625 --> 00:16:37,375
Khan brother! Khan brother! - He has a cleaver!

448
00:16:38,541 --> 00:16:39,375
Khan brother!

449
00:16:39,416 --> 00:16:41,416
Shir-Ali! Shir-Ali!

450
00:16:41,458 --> 00:16:42,833
Enough already! - Open the door!

451
00:16:42,875 --> 00:16:44,791
Shir-Ali, for God's sake let him go!

452
00:16:45,708 --> 00:16:48,666
What shameless people exist in this world!

453
00:16:48,708 --> 00:16:50,416
Why go into other people's houses!

454
00:16:50,458 --> 00:16:52,833
Don't you have any honor yourself, Dustali!

455
00:16:52,875 --> 00:16:54,791
That you violate other people's honor!

456
00:16:54,791 --> 00:16:55,708
Asdollah!

457
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:58,291
You shut up already!

458
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:00,125
Moment! Moment! - Get up...

459
00:17:00,166 --> 00:17:01,875
Then let me go open the door

460
00:17:01,875 --> 00:17:02,416
and ask

461
00:17:02,458 --> 00:17:04,833
who exactly Shir-Ali is after.

462
00:17:04,875 --> 00:17:05,541
I beg you!

463
00:17:05,583 --> 00:17:06,208
Mr. Shir-Ali! - Don't let him go!

464
00:17:06,208 --> 00:17:08,208
Mr. Shir-Ali, wait a minute, I'm opening the door now.

465
00:17:08,208 --> 00:17:09,500
- That bear is going to kill me!

466
00:17:09,541 --> 00:17:11,833
(Crowd murmur)

467
00:17:11,875 --> 00:17:13,666
So now you're a lecher and a bully too?

468
00:17:13,666 --> 00:17:18,333
(Crowd murmur)

469
00:17:18,375 --> 00:17:19,500
Shameless!

470
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:20,791
Shame on you!

471
00:17:20,791 --> 00:17:21,875
(Crowd murmur)

472
00:17:21,916 --> 00:17:22,666
Die!

473
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:25,750
(Crowd murmur)

474
00:17:29,041 --> 00:17:29,750
I'll kill him!

475
00:17:29,791 --> 00:17:30,791
Let me go!

476
00:17:30,791 --> 00:17:31,833
Let me go!

477
00:17:32,250 --> 00:17:33,125
Bastard!

478
00:17:33,166 --> 00:17:34,166
- Forgive him!

479
00:17:34,583 --> 00:17:36,541
- Be the bigger man, forgive him!

480
00:17:36,541 --> 00:17:37,458
Why should I

481
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:39,000
go to all this trouble?!

482
00:17:39,041 --> 00:17:41,625
I'm opening the door so that cleaver-wielder...

483
00:17:41,625 --> 00:17:45,125
(Crowd murmur)

484
00:17:45,166 --> 00:17:47,000
- Don't let him open the door!

485
00:17:47,416 --> 00:17:49,083
If that brute comes in,

486
00:17:49,375 --> 00:17:51,250
he wants to kill me!

487
00:17:51,291 --> 00:17:52,416
I'll deal with you right now!

488
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:55,291
Shir-Ali!

489
00:17:55,333 --> 00:17:56,083
Shir-Ali!

490
00:17:56,125 --> 00:17:57,291
For my sake forgive him!

491
00:17:57,666 --> 00:17:58,416
Shir-Ali!

492
00:17:58,458 --> 00:18:00,625
Shir-Ali, don't kill him!

493
00:18:00,666 --> 00:18:03,666
(Crowd murmur)

494
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,125
Stop him! He has a cleaver!

495
00:18:08,125 --> 00:18:09,833
Get out of the way!

496
00:18:10,833 --> 00:18:12,791
Where are you, coward!

497
00:18:13,125 --> 00:18:15,500
My quarrel isn't with you...

498
00:18:15,750 --> 00:18:18,333
It's this dishonorable wretch I want!

499
00:18:18,791 --> 00:18:20,625
Hey! (Airplane sound heard in the sky)

500
00:18:20,750 --> 00:18:22,541
All of you get out of the way! (Airplane sound heard in the sky)

501
00:18:22,625 --> 00:18:24,708
It's that coward I want!

502
00:18:24,833 --> 00:18:26,833
(Airplane sound heard in the sky)

503
00:18:30,833 --> 00:18:32,416
Sir, what's that sound!

504
00:18:32,875 --> 00:18:34,166
Do you hear that?

505
00:18:39,750 --> 00:18:40,791
What's that sound? - It's a plane!

506
00:18:40,875 --> 00:18:42,708
Sounds like a plane!

507
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:43,625
Sir!

508
00:18:43,916 --> 00:18:44,291
Huh?

509
00:18:44,291 --> 00:18:44,958
Sir!

510
00:18:45,291 --> 00:18:46,833
The British have attacked!

511
00:18:47,375 --> 00:18:47,833
Huh?

512
00:18:47,833 --> 00:18:49,958
Quick, do something to save yourself.

513
00:18:52,375 --> 00:18:53,708
The British have come!

514
00:18:53,750 --> 00:18:58,083
(Sound of screams and chaos)

515
00:18:58,458 --> 00:19:00,375
- War! War has started!

516
00:19:01,041 --> 00:19:03,041
(Air raid siren sound)

517
00:19:14,375 --> 00:19:16,375
♪ Traditional music ♪

518
00:20:02,708 --> 00:20:03,583
Be careful!

519
00:20:04,083 --> 00:20:05,500
Don't stack them on top of each other.

520
00:20:07,833 --> 00:20:09,208
Don't stack them on top of each other!

521
00:20:13,125 --> 00:20:14,166
Put it over there.

522
00:20:14,333 --> 00:20:15,041
Over there.

523
00:20:15,083 --> 00:20:15,750
Yeah!

524
00:20:15,958 --> 00:20:17,083
It's gone cold.

525
00:20:17,208 --> 00:20:18,791
Now leave it for a minute, come drink your tea.

526
00:20:18,791 --> 00:20:20,291
Okay, later... I'm not hungry.

527
00:20:20,333 --> 00:20:21,833
Hurry up already!

528
00:20:31,041 --> 00:20:32,041
I'm talking to you!

529
00:20:32,041 --> 00:20:33,250
Take it and put it there.

530
00:20:33,583 --> 00:20:35,375
Take it and put it by the door.

531
00:20:35,666 --> 00:20:37,375
What kind of work is this!

532
00:20:37,416 --> 00:20:38,375
Hurry up!

533
00:20:41,375 --> 00:20:43,666
♪ Last night when the blackout happened in Tehran ♪ (Radio announcer's voice)

534
00:20:43,708 --> 00:20:46,000
Quick! Quick, take it and put it in front of the door. ♪ And there was a possibility of an air raid ♪

535
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,041
Hey! Those are fragile! ♪ The order of the city was completely disrupted ♪

536
00:20:48,083 --> 00:20:49,416
Be a little careful! ♪ With the closing of cinemas, ♪

537
00:20:49,500 --> 00:20:50,750
Oh man... Aqa Jan! ♪ And with the rush of the crowd, ♪

538
00:20:50,750 --> 00:20:51,958
You go, I'll watch. ♪ And people fleeing to their homes ♪

539
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,875
Unless you stand over them, they won't work! ♪ created an uncomfortable situation. ♪

540
00:20:53,875 --> 00:20:55,375
♪ Especially for women and children ♪

541
00:20:55,458 --> 00:20:57,666
♪ and elderly men who didn't have the ability to run, ♪

542
00:20:58,333 --> 00:21:00,375
♪ and get out of the way of the crowd ♪

543
00:21:00,500 --> 00:21:02,958
♪ in the streets and alleys. ♪

544
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,791
Slower! The glasses are in those boxes! ♪ The Ministry of Interior's instructions for, ♪

545
00:21:05,041 --> 00:21:07,291
Be careful it doesn't fall! ♪ protecting people's lives in case of bombing, ♪

546
00:21:07,666 --> 00:21:08,458
A little slower! ♪ can be heard. ♪

