579
00:22:13,458 --> 00:22:13,958
No...

580
00:22:15,541 --> 00:22:16,833
I hope all's well, Khan brother.

581
00:22:18,541 --> 00:22:20,541
Would you like some tea? Shall I bring it for you?

582
00:22:22,375 --> 00:22:24,458
No sister, don't trouble yourself.

583
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:27,791
It's too late for your brother to drink tea!

584
00:22:28,083 --> 00:22:30,083
♪ Tombak drumming ♪

585
00:22:32,833 --> 00:22:33,916
Oh God!

586
00:22:35,625 --> 00:22:37,791
What's happened now, so early in the morning?

587
00:23:01,041 --> 00:23:02,166
This morning at dawn,

588
00:23:02,208 --> 00:23:05,166
the Allies attacked from the north and south!

589
00:23:05,416 --> 00:23:08,000
The government hasn't said a word yet!

590
00:23:08,208 --> 00:23:10,125
I knew that eventually,

591
00:23:10,166 --> 00:23:11,875
the British would make their move!

592
00:23:12,041 --> 00:23:16,375
I'm not the kind of person who dies a natural death!

593
00:23:16,416 --> 00:23:20,333
I don't even trust my own brother and sister!

594
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:22,666
That's why I came to share my decision

595
00:23:22,750 --> 00:23:24,875
with you.

596
00:23:25,250 --> 00:23:28,458
You've always been like a brother to me.

597
00:23:28,750 --> 00:23:31,166
Even now I expect you to help me.

598
00:23:31,291 --> 00:23:33,125
Do me this favor.

599
00:23:33,708 --> 00:23:35,500
Honestly, no matter how much I think about it,

600
00:23:35,541 --> 00:23:37,250
on one hand I see you are right!

601
00:23:38,166 --> 00:23:39,750
Staying here is not advisable at all!

602
00:23:39,916 --> 00:23:40,916
On the other hand...

603
00:23:41,208 --> 00:23:43,125
Leaving Tehran is also very difficult!

604
00:23:43,458 --> 00:23:44,458
What will you do with Lily and Mash Ghasem and...

605
00:23:45,083 --> 00:23:46,583
your home and household?

606
00:23:46,875 --> 00:23:48,375
What will you do with your home and household?

607
00:23:48,625 --> 00:23:50,666
I'm leaving today.

608
00:23:50,958 --> 00:23:52,708
You arrange for them to leave

609
00:23:52,750 --> 00:23:53,583
a few days later.

610
00:23:53,791 --> 00:23:56,291
But make sure no one notices!

611
00:23:56,541 --> 00:23:59,500
Especially this Indian who is your tenant!

612
00:24:00,416 --> 00:24:03,416
I didn't expect such carelessness from you!

613
00:24:03,458 --> 00:24:05,000
What are you saying, Sir?

614
00:24:05,125 --> 00:24:06,541
I'm being careful.

615
00:24:07,041 --> 00:24:09,875
This Indian is a very good man, he's a merchant.

616
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,250
I'm sure,

617
00:24:11,291 --> 00:24:14,458
that the British specifically made this Indian

618
00:24:14,708 --> 00:24:16,083
rent this place,

619
00:24:16,250 --> 00:24:18,541
to keep an eye on me!

620
00:24:18,791 --> 00:24:21,500
They say his wife is English too, right?

621
00:24:22,416 --> 00:24:24,750
Yes! But rest assured.

622
00:24:25,208 --> 00:24:27,583
To be honest, I didn't even know this Indian myself.

623
00:24:28,083 --> 00:24:30,041
I didn't want to rent the house to him.

624
00:24:30,583 --> 00:24:33,458
But Asdollah Mirza insisted so much that I had no choice.

625
00:24:35,333 --> 00:24:36,625
He said this poor man,

626
00:24:36,666 --> 00:24:39,416
is alone, a stranger, our guest...

627
00:24:39,625 --> 00:24:41,916
The poor guy has been out of touch with his family,

628
00:24:41,958 --> 00:24:43,000
his mother,

629
00:24:43,041 --> 00:24:43,708
his father,

630
00:24:43,750 --> 00:24:44,875
for a long time.

631
00:24:46,166 --> 00:24:48,666
Especially now that there's war all over the world.

632
00:24:50,291 --> 00:24:52,833
To be honest, I trusted Asdollah Mirza's words.

633
00:24:52,875 --> 00:24:55,125
After all, he works at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

634
00:24:56,916 --> 00:24:57,958
If I'm not mistaken,

635
00:24:58,250 --> 00:25:00,125
Asdollah must have something going on with this Indian's wife,

636
00:25:00,291 --> 00:25:01,416
You shouldn't think too much about these things.

637
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,500
Now that you've decided to leave Tehran,

638
00:25:04,333 --> 00:25:07,041
first you need to think about a driver

639
00:25:07,458 --> 00:25:09,250
who will take you.

640
00:25:09,291 --> 00:25:10,166
He won't stay with you forever!

641
00:25:10,750 --> 00:25:12,458
He'll eventually return!

642
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:13,666
How do we know he won't reveal your hiding place?

643
00:25:14,041 --> 00:25:16,708
The driver doesn't worry me.

644
00:25:23,958 --> 00:25:25,958
I'm going in Dabir Khaghan's car,

645
00:25:26,125 --> 00:25:27,958
his driver served for years

646
00:25:29,750 --> 00:25:31,416
under my command.

647
00:25:31,625 --> 00:25:32,583
In the wars,

648
00:25:33,083 --> 00:25:35,458
he'd give his life for me.

649
00:25:35,833 --> 00:25:38,458
He's like another Ghasem to me.

650
00:25:38,541 --> 00:25:39,666
Even so,

651
00:25:39,666 --> 00:25:42,250
I believe you should wait one or two more days,

652
00:25:42,250 --> 00:25:44,250
to carefully consider all aspects of the matter.

653
00:25:44,375 --> 00:25:45,750
No! No! No!

654
00:25:48,833 --> 00:25:50,708
Slower! Put it down slower!

655
00:25:52,708 --> 00:25:54,625
They won't wait!

656
00:25:54,791 --> 00:25:58,125
The British army has attacked the south of the country!

657
00:25:58,500 --> 00:26:01,291
With the means they have, it's quite possible

658
00:26:01,291 --> 00:26:04,416
if they entered Tehran today or tomorrow!

659
00:26:04,583 --> 00:26:08,250
We must not let the opportunity slip away!

660
00:26:08,666 --> 00:26:12,166
Believe me, I'm not thinking about myself!

661
00:26:12,375 --> 00:26:16,708
Everyone knows that I have lived with danger.

662
00:26:16,791 --> 00:26:19,291
I am used to danger!

663
00:26:20,250 --> 00:26:22,166
As Napoleon said:

664
00:26:22,333 --> 00:26:26,000
Great men are the children of danger.

665
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:29,541
I'm thinking about Lily!

666
00:26:29,666 --> 00:26:32,791
I'm thinking about your children!

667
00:26:33,708 --> 00:26:35,041
I'm sure,

668
00:26:35,083 --> 00:26:37,000
last night their planes

669
00:26:37,125 --> 00:26:39,791
wanted to bomb my house!

670
00:26:39,875 --> 00:26:41,250
Do you think

671
00:26:41,250 --> 00:26:43,583
that last night's blackout and noise

672
00:26:43,625 --> 00:26:45,625
was just a practice for an air raid?

673
00:26:45,666 --> 00:26:47,166
By God's grace,

674
00:26:47,250 --> 00:26:50,041
they got it wrong in the dark!

675
00:26:50,125 --> 00:26:52,958
Now that their plan didn't work,

676
00:26:53,125 --> 00:26:56,291
be sure that as soon as they enter Tehran,

677
00:26:56,583 --> 00:26:58,916
the first thing they will do

678
00:26:59,333 --> 00:27:02,916
is settle their old scores with me!

679
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:07,458
I know the British are very vengeful.

680
00:27:07,791 --> 00:27:10,250
They never forget an old score!

681
00:27:10,750 --> 00:27:12,916
But do you think we can fool them?

682
00:27:13,375 --> 00:27:15,541
Do you think if you go to Nishapur,

683
00:27:15,583 --> 00:27:16,916
you will be safe and sound?

684
00:27:17,125 --> 00:27:17,958
First of all!

685
00:27:18,458 --> 00:27:20,125
Six of these bullets are for them!

686
00:27:20,166 --> 00:27:21,375
The last one is for myself!

687
00:27:21,666 --> 00:27:24,291
They will never be able to capture me alive!

688
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:25,666
Secondly!

689
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:27,166
From here,

690
00:27:27,875 --> 00:27:30,000
I will head for Qom.

691
00:27:30,541 --> 00:27:31,958
No one, do you hear?

692
00:27:32,125 --> 00:27:33,166
No one!

693
00:27:33,250 --> 00:27:36,000
Not even my loyal driver,

694
00:27:36,041 --> 00:27:38,208
knows my real destination!

695
00:27:39,125 --> 00:27:42,083
I'll tell even him we're going to Qom!

696
00:27:42,416 --> 00:27:45,000
Once we pass through the city gate,

697
00:27:45,333 --> 00:27:47,583
we'll turn off toward Nishapur!

698
00:27:47,791 --> 00:27:49,750
When you reach Nishapur, what will you do?

699
00:27:50,458 --> 00:27:53,166
Huh? Do you think the British don't have spies there?

700
00:27:54,458 --> 00:27:56,416
Dabir Khaghan's village,

701
00:27:56,708 --> 00:27:59,041
is about twelve miles outside Nishapur.

702
00:27:59,875 --> 00:28:00,625
Besides!

703
00:28:01,083 --> 00:28:04,041
And there I plan to go under a false name,

704
00:28:04,041 --> 00:28:05,583
then we'll see what happens!

705
00:28:07,666 --> 00:28:08,958
High or low?

706
00:28:09,208 --> 00:28:10,416
Low!

707
00:28:11,958 --> 00:28:12,791
I'm rolling!

708
00:28:18,416 --> 00:28:19,416
Halt!

709
00:28:20,541 --> 00:28:21,458
Is that you Mash Ghasem?

710
00:28:22,166 --> 00:28:23,541
What are you doing up there?

711
00:28:23,750 --> 00:28:25,000
Don't move!

712
00:28:25,416 --> 00:28:26,625
You scared me Mash Ghasem!

713
00:28:27,958 --> 00:28:29,500
Honestly, kid, why lie!

714
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:31,750
I've one foot in the grave!

715
00:28:32,041 --> 00:28:33,958
Our days are numbered!

716
00:28:35,125 --> 00:28:36,583
God forbid Mash Ghasem.

717
00:28:38,375 --> 00:28:39,583
We, too, of course,

718
00:28:39,625 --> 00:28:41,083
not as many as Sir,

719
00:28:41,166 --> 00:28:42,833
but as best we could,

720
00:28:42,833 --> 00:28:43,958
in the Kazerun war,

721
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:46,125
killed plenty of British soldiers!

722
00:28:46,791 --> 00:28:49,291
They won't forget this for another 100 years.

723
00:28:50,416 --> 00:28:52,500
We've been on guard since last night!

724
00:28:52,708 --> 00:28:54,583
If the British army comes,

725
00:28:54,750 --> 00:28:56,583
we'll kill as many as we can,

726
00:28:56,583 --> 00:28:57,958
until we're killed ourselves!

727
00:28:59,500 --> 00:29:00,000
Kid!

728
00:29:00,583 --> 00:29:01,916
Where were you going?

729
00:29:01,958 --> 00:29:03,583
M... m... m... me!

730
00:29:03,666 --> 00:29:05,000
Sir has forbidden

731
00:29:05,041 --> 00:29:06,625
anyone to leave by the garden gate.

732
00:29:07,375 --> 00:29:08,791
If someone goes out,

733
00:29:08,833 --> 00:29:09,750
we tell them to halt.

734
00:29:09,958 --> 00:29:11,041
If they don't stop,

735
00:29:11,083 --> 00:29:12,833
we will shoot them until they stop!

736
00:29:13,208 --> 00:29:14,791
I have a mission to go to the gate,

737
00:29:14,833 --> 00:29:15,791
to see if the British army's

738
00:29:15,791 --> 00:29:17,333
dust cloud is visible or not!

739
00:29:17,625 --> 00:29:18,583
And if it is,

740
00:29:18,583 --> 00:29:20,291
I'll signal you from far off!

741
00:29:25,708 --> 00:29:26,625
Kid!

742
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:28,333
When you give the signal,

743
00:29:28,375 --> 00:29:29,375
get out of the way quickly.

744
00:29:29,583 --> 00:29:31,250
So our bullets don't hit you.

745
00:29:32,625 --> 00:29:33,291
This way.

746
00:29:41,083 --> 00:29:41,875
Be careful!

747
00:29:47,208 --> 00:29:48,458
Come in this way please!

748
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:52,250
- Bamieh!

749
00:29:55,083 --> 00:29:56,750
Are you blind? - Watch your step, man!

750
00:30:04,083 --> 00:30:06,333
- Fresh bamieh!

751
00:30:07,791 --> 00:30:09,041
- Bamieh.

752
00:30:12,750 --> 00:30:13,458
Who is it?

753
00:30:13,625 --> 00:30:14,541
It's me! Saeed.

754
00:30:16,500 --> 00:30:17,500
I'm coming.

755
00:30:18,458 --> 00:30:19,583
Granny! Open the door, quick!

756
00:30:20,875 --> 00:30:21,625
Hello Sir!

757
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:23,833
Is Uncle Asdollah here or did he go to the office?

758
00:30:23,875 --> 00:30:24,458
I think he's sleeping.

759
00:30:24,500 --> 00:30:26,000
Granny dear! Go wake him up, quick.

760
00:30:26,041 --> 00:30:26,375
Very well!

761
00:30:26,416 --> 00:30:27,333
Saeed! - Uncle Asdollah, hello!

762
00:30:27,375 --> 00:30:29,166
What are you doing here so early in the morning?

763
00:30:29,166 --> 00:30:30,666
I need you for something important.

764
00:30:30,791 --> 00:30:32,375
Tell me! What happened?

765
00:30:32,416 --> 00:30:34,041
Uncle Asdollah, how long will this trip take?

766
00:30:34,125 --> 00:30:35,083
Which trip?

767
00:30:35,125 --> 00:30:36,083
I'm not going anywhere!

768
00:30:36,083 --> 00:30:36,750
I'm not talking about you!

769
00:30:36,750 --> 00:30:38,916
Lily! Lily wants to go on a trip!

770
00:30:39,333 --> 00:30:40,541
You came just to say this?

771
00:30:40,875 --> 00:30:41,333
You go.

772
00:30:41,458 --> 00:30:42,000
Yes!

773
00:30:43,250 --> 00:30:44,791
Congratulations!

774
00:30:45,625 --> 00:30:47,416
You're hooked on Lily, aren't you?

775
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:48,958
Are you or not?

776
00:30:48,958 --> 00:30:50,416
Answer me! Quick, fast, hurry!

777
00:30:50,708 --> 00:30:52,291
It's been a long time, Uncle Asdollah!

778
00:30:52,583 --> 00:30:54,583
If you took her to San Francisco, tell Uncle!

779
00:30:54,583 --> 00:30:55,791
No!

780
00:30:56,333 --> 00:30:58,500
I bet you're looking for one of those midwives now,

781
00:30:58,541 --> 00:31:00,125
to get rid of the baby!

782
00:31:00,666 --> 00:31:01,375
Don't worry about that!

783
00:31:01,416 --> 00:31:02,500
I know ten of them!

784
00:31:02,500 --> 00:31:03,625
No, Uncle Asdollah!

785
00:31:03,666 --> 00:31:05,125
I actually came here for something else!

786
00:31:05,166 --> 00:31:06,166
So no San Francisco then!

787
00:31:06,291 --> 00:31:07,625
Answer me, quick, fast, hurry!

788
00:31:07,666 --> 00:31:08,416
Has it happened or not?

789
00:31:08,458 --> 00:31:10,250
No, Uncle Asdollah! No, no!

790
00:31:10,333 --> 00:31:11,458
So you're sweethearts who just want to play jacks together?

791
00:31:12,916 --> 00:31:14,666
We want to get married later, after we finish our studies!

792
00:31:14,708 --> 00:31:15,750
By the time you finish your studies,

793
00:31:16,291 --> 00:31:17,958
Lily will have given birth to three kids!

794
00:31:17,958 --> 00:31:19,500
If you want Lily to stay with you,

795
00:31:20,083 --> 00:31:21,333
Think of something else!

796
00:31:21,333 --> 00:31:22,666
What should I think of, Uncle Asdollah?

797
00:31:23,500 --> 00:31:24,875
You must pop over to San Francisco

798
00:31:25,708 --> 00:31:27,458
and back!

799
00:31:27,458 --> 00:31:28,458
You always joke with me.

800
00:31:28,708 --> 00:31:30,041
Please, show me a way out.

801
00:31:30,041 --> 00:31:31,666
If I can't ruin Uncle's trip,

802
00:31:31,958 --> 00:31:33,666
Lily will go with him too!

803
00:31:33,708 --> 00:31:34,625
Is Uncle going on a trip!?

804
00:31:36,458 --> 00:31:38,375
Where?

805
00:31:38,708 --> 00:31:39,125
Uncle is imagining things!

806
00:31:39,166 --> 00:31:40,375
He's so afraid of a British attack, he wants to flee.

807
00:31:40,500 --> 00:31:42,500
Go out to the courtyard.

808
00:31:45,166 --> 00:31:46,375
Wait there till I change,

809
00:31:46,583 --> 00:31:47,916
Uncle Asdollah!

810
00:31:47,916 --> 00:31:48,500
Can you do something so Uncle doesn't go on the trip?

811
00:31:48,500 --> 00:31:50,083
Saghi!

812
00:32:01,625 --> 00:32:02,208
Soghra!

813
00:32:02,541 --> 00:32:03,166
Come on!

814
00:32:03,416 --> 00:32:04,625
Moment!

815
00:32:04,666 --> 00:32:05,750
Moment!

816
00:32:06,041 --> 00:32:08,583
Okay! What is it! Let me put on my chador!

817
00:32:10,291 --> 00:32:11,500
Who's come, anyway? Go on, go, go!

818
00:32:11,500 --> 00:32:13,125
Go so no one sees you! Go, go! What do you care!

819
00:32:19,083 --> 00:32:20,041
Saeed Khan!

820
00:32:23,625 --> 00:32:25,833
I've poured you tea, go in and drink it.

821
00:32:26,750 --> 00:32:27,416
Your uncle,

822
00:32:27,416 --> 00:32:28,750
Even if Churchill himself comes,

823
00:32:28,791 --> 00:32:30,708
and swears by 124,000 prophets,

824
00:32:30,750 --> 00:32:33,125
that he has no quarrel with a retired lieutenant of the Cossack Brigade,

825
00:32:33,208 --> 00:32:34,000
he still won't believe it!

826
00:32:34,083 --> 00:32:35,541
Now where does he want to go?

827
00:32:35,916 --> 00:32:38,583
He's sure the British will forgive Hitler's sins,

828
00:32:38,625 --> 00:32:40,166
but they won't forgive his!

829
00:32:40,208 --> 00:32:41,041
Now where does he want to go?

830
00:32:41,250 --> 00:32:42,125
They're going to Qom.

831
00:32:42,458 --> 00:32:42,833
I mean...

832
00:32:43,666 --> 00:32:45,125
They set out for Qom,

833
00:32:45,333 --> 00:32:46,750
but then they go to Nishapur.

834
00:32:46,875 --> 00:32:47,875
By a shortcut.

835
00:32:47,916 --> 00:32:49,041
Does anyone else know,

836
00:32:49,083 --> 00:32:50,375
that Sir wants to go to Nishapur?

837
00:32:50,625 --> 00:32:51,583
No, Uncle Asdollah!

838
00:32:51,625 --> 00:32:53,333
Only me and Aqa Jan know this!

839
00:32:53,333 --> 00:32:53,958
They told everyone,

840
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:56,166
they're going on a pilgrimage in Dabir Khaghan's car.

841
00:32:57,000 --> 00:32:57,666
If they go,

842
00:32:58,083 --> 00:33:00,333
if they go, I won't be able to see Lily anymore!

843
00:33:00,333 --> 00:33:02,208
Moment! Moment!

844
00:33:02,208 --> 00:33:03,958
So if the British find out,

845
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:06,708
that Sir, instead of Qom, wants to go to Nishapur,

846
00:33:06,750 --> 00:33:08,666
he'll surely give up the trip.

847
00:33:08,958 --> 00:33:09,375
Aha!

848
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:11,791
We must act before it's too late!

849
00:33:12,166 --> 00:33:13,750
We must make the British understand

850
00:33:13,791 --> 00:33:16,000
that Sir wants to flee to Nishapur!

851
00:33:16,833 --> 00:33:19,083
On the other hand, Sir himself must learn

852
00:33:19,125 --> 00:33:21,208
that the British have figured it out!

853
00:33:21,833 --> 00:33:22,125
This way,

854
00:33:22,125 --> 00:33:24,666
perhaps we can save the poor British too!

855
00:33:25,416 --> 00:33:27,000
Otherwise they'll have to,

856
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:29,208
send a special bomber plane

857
00:33:29,250 --> 00:33:30,291
from London

858
00:33:30,291 --> 00:33:32,250
to bomb Dabir Khaghan's car

859
00:33:32,291 --> 00:33:34,916
in the twists and turns of the Thousand Valleys road!

860
00:33:36,500 --> 00:33:37,583
Of course,

861
00:33:37,625 --> 00:33:38,250
a great danger

862
00:33:38,291 --> 00:33:40,458
threatens the plane and the pilot!

863
00:33:41,125 --> 00:33:42,000
Before you know it,

864
00:33:42,041 --> 00:33:43,833
Sir, the champion shooter,

865
00:33:43,875 --> 00:33:44,333
with his double-barrel,

866
00:33:44,791 --> 00:33:45,375
Bang!

867
00:33:45,375 --> 00:33:47,416
he's maimed the pilot's noble member!

868
00:33:47,458 --> 00:33:49,291
(They laugh)

869
00:34:25,083 --> 00:34:26,291
Well...

870
00:34:26,750 --> 00:34:28,041
So tell me, kid...

871
00:34:28,958 --> 00:34:31,041
Does Lily like you too?

872
00:34:31,833 --> 00:34:33,291
Lily loves me very much.

873
00:34:33,500 --> 00:34:34,666
But promise me,

874
00:34:34,708 --> 00:34:35,833
don't tell anyone!

875
00:34:36,500 --> 00:34:37,500
If Uncle finds out,

876
00:34:37,541 --> 00:34:39,000
he won't let us see each other anymore.

877
00:34:39,916 --> 00:34:40,791
Saeed!

878
00:34:42,166 --> 00:34:43,208
Rest assured.

879
00:34:46,208 --> 00:34:47,958
When did you fall for her?

880
00:34:48,541 --> 00:34:49,708
On the thirteenth of Mordad.

881
00:34:52,333 --> 00:34:54,625
You probably know the exact time too!

882
00:34:55,208 --> 00:34:56,125
A quarter to three.

883
00:34:57,958 --> 00:34:58,500
Listen!

884
00:34:58,958 --> 00:35:00,166
I have a few pieces of advice.

885
00:35:01,458 --> 00:35:01,958
First!

886
00:35:02,125 --> 00:35:04,083
Don't show her that you like her too much.

887
00:35:04,458 --> 00:35:05,000
Second!

888
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:06,625
If,

889
00:35:06,791 --> 00:35:08,333
you see she's slipping away from you,

890
00:35:08,375 --> 00:35:10,125
don't forget San Francisco!

891
00:35:10,166 --> 00:35:11,500
Uncle Asdollah!

892
00:35:14,291 --> 00:35:15,500
I have a plan,

893
00:35:15,500 --> 00:35:16,875
to keep Lily from being taken from you!

894
00:35:17,666 --> 00:35:18,375
Are you sure?

895
00:35:19,208 --> 00:35:20,166
Sure.

896
00:35:20,833 --> 00:35:22,791
But what will you do about that spluttering Puri?

897
00:35:23,625 --> 00:35:24,875
You must have heard.

898
00:35:25,291 --> 00:35:27,208
Once Pouri finishes his military service,

899
00:35:27,291 --> 00:35:29,041
they plan to celebrate his engagement with Lily.

900
00:35:30,208 --> 00:35:31,041
Lily herself,

901
00:35:31,458 --> 00:35:33,041
suddenly wrote in her note,

902
00:35:33,083 --> 00:35:35,541
that she might be forced to become Pouri's wife.

903
00:35:36,416 --> 00:35:38,083
So you're exchanging notes too!

904
00:35:38,291 --> 00:35:39,208
What did she write?

905
00:35:39,250 --> 00:35:40,166
Quick, fast, immediately!

906
00:35:40,416 --> 00:35:41,333
Answer!

907
00:35:41,666 --> 00:35:42,541
She wrote...

908
00:35:43,166 --> 00:35:45,000
If they force her to become Pouri's wife,

909
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:46,125
she'll kill herself!

910
00:35:46,166 --> 00:35:48,166
(Asdollah laughs)

911
00:35:48,833 --> 00:35:49,333
Well!

912
00:35:49,750 --> 00:35:50,958
To the British army!

913
00:35:51,208 --> 00:35:52,666
For the rescue of a hero, forward!

914
00:35:53,083 --> 00:35:53,958
March!

915
00:35:54,125 --> 00:35:55,541
One... two... one

916
00:36:00,166 --> 00:36:02,458
Don't worry too much!

917
00:36:02,500 --> 00:36:03,250
Don't be sad.

918
00:36:03,666 --> 00:36:05,416
God helps lovers.

919
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:10,875
(Traditional music)

920
00:36:27,458 --> 00:36:28,083
I understand!

921
00:36:28,541 --> 00:36:29,000
I understand!

922
00:36:29,083 --> 00:36:29,583
There he is!

923
00:36:29,583 --> 00:36:30,875
He's still keeping watch!

924
00:36:30,958 --> 00:36:32,458
Well, don't let on, kid...

925
00:36:32,541 --> 00:36:33,583
Well, well, Mash Ghasem!

926
00:36:33,625 --> 00:36:34,750
Any fresh news?

927
00:36:36,208 --> 00:36:37,708
Honestly Sir, why lie!

928
00:36:37,833 --> 00:36:39,041
We don't have good news.

929
00:36:39,041 --> 00:36:40,833
Sir is planning to go to Qom.

930
00:36:41,208 --> 00:36:42,458
Good for Sir!

931
00:36:42,500 --> 00:36:43,875
That's not bad news.

932
00:36:43,916 --> 00:36:46,125
(Sound of children playing)

933
00:36:47,375 --> 00:36:48,666
We begged and begged Sir

934
00:36:48,708 --> 00:36:50,041
to take us with him,

935
00:36:50,083 --> 00:36:51,541
so we could visit Ghiyas Abad,

936
00:36:51,583 --> 00:36:52,958
but Sir wouldn't agree.

937
00:36:54,125 --> 00:36:55,416
Well... what can be done!

938
00:36:55,458 --> 00:36:57,916
Lady Masoumeh must have called Sir to Qom,

939
00:36:57,958 --> 00:36:59,125
but not us.

940
00:36:59,250 --> 00:37:00,375
How are they traveling?

941
00:37:00,416 --> 00:37:02,083
By train or by car?

942
00:37:03,333 --> 00:37:04,583
Honestly, why lie!

943
00:37:04,625 --> 00:37:06,083
By car, I think.

944
00:37:06,750 --> 00:37:09,750
We heard them phoning Mr. Dabir Khaghan,

945
00:37:09,750 --> 00:37:10,500
to send the car,

946
00:37:10,541 --> 00:37:12,000
along with Mohammad Aqa, their driver,

947
00:37:12,041 --> 00:37:13,125
to come here.

948
00:37:13,125 --> 00:37:13,875
Aha!

949
00:37:13,916 --> 00:37:15,125
When are they leaving?

950
00:37:15,500 --> 00:37:16,708
This afternoon, I think,

951
00:37:16,750 --> 00:37:18,041
when the weather cools down.

952
00:37:18,666 --> 00:37:19,791
Kid!

953
00:37:20,041 --> 00:37:21,833
You didn't go to the gate?

954
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:23,958
Yes, Mash Ghasem.

955
00:37:23,958 --> 00:37:25,041
They hadn't come yet!

956
00:37:25,250 --> 00:37:25,875
Kid,

957
00:37:25,875 --> 00:37:27,625
today from up here we saw

958
00:37:27,958 --> 00:37:30,000
a cloud of dust rise!

959
00:37:30,500 --> 00:37:32,375
Now Mash Ghasem! Take another look!

960
00:37:32,416 --> 00:37:32,791
See,

961
00:37:32,791 --> 00:37:33,833
do you see anything?

962
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:34,666
Right away!

963
00:37:38,875 --> 00:37:40,166
Nothing visible on this side.

964
00:37:45,208 --> 00:37:46,083
Hey, come...

965
00:37:50,666 --> 00:37:51,583
This way, this way.

966
00:37:51,583 --> 00:37:52,166
Where are we going?

967
00:37:52,166 --> 00:37:52,708
Come, come!

968
00:37:53,375 --> 00:37:54,000
Uncle Asdollah!

969
00:37:54,083 --> 00:37:55,375
What are we doing at Sardar's house?

970
00:37:55,625 --> 00:37:57,541
Come on, mind your own business!

971
00:37:57,750 --> 00:37:58,666
(knocking on the door)

972
00:37:58,875 --> 00:38:00,083
Moment!

973
00:38:04,708 --> 00:38:05,500
Oh!

974
00:38:05,708 --> 00:38:06,541
Good morning!

975
00:38:06,583 --> 00:38:07,291
It's you!

976
00:38:07,500 --> 00:38:09,000
Good morning Mr Asdollah!

977
00:38:09,458 --> 00:38:11,208
Excuse me for disturbing you,

978
00:38:11,250 --> 00:38:12,625
so early in the morning!

979
00:38:12,750 --> 00:38:14,125
Is your husband in?

980
00:38:14,625 --> 00:38:15,791
He went out shopping.

981
00:38:15,875 --> 00:38:16,750
He will be back.

982
00:38:17,125 --> 00:38:17,875
Please come in.

983
00:38:18,166 --> 00:38:19,291
What a surprise!

984
00:38:19,791 --> 00:38:21,791
Uncle Asdollah! Why did we come here?

985
00:38:21,833 --> 00:38:23,750
Moment! Moment!

986
00:38:23,791 --> 00:38:24,708
Wait, boy!

987
00:38:24,750 --> 00:38:25,625
I've taken a liking to you,

988
00:38:25,625 --> 00:38:28,333
I'm going on a trip with this lady to San Francisco!

989
00:38:30,041 --> 00:38:31,916
Sorry. I didn't bring you flowers. - Come in! Come in!

990
00:38:31,958 --> 00:38:32,750
Saeed, go inside!

991
00:38:33,166 --> 00:38:34,375
I was in a hurry.

992
00:38:34,458 --> 00:38:36,000
Oh, that's gotta be alright.

993
00:38:39,208 --> 00:38:39,791
Thank you!

994
00:38:39,833 --> 00:38:40,625
Come in! Come in!

995
00:38:47,416 --> 00:38:48,958
Make yourself comfortable.

996
00:38:51,500 --> 00:38:53,333
What a lovely house!

997
00:38:53,916 --> 00:38:54,916
Found it yourself!

998
00:38:56,541 --> 00:38:57,541
Will you drink some wine?

999
00:38:58,791 --> 00:39:00,375
That early in the morning?

1000
00:39:00,958 --> 00:39:02,583
There's no wrong time for good wine!

1001
00:39:04,708 --> 00:39:05,291
Well,

1002
00:39:05,291 --> 00:39:06,750
we will drink then!

1003
00:39:10,166 --> 00:39:10,958
Yes.

1004
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:16,333
I think Sardar is coming.

1005
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:19,833
Yes!

1006
00:39:21,041 --> 00:39:21,916
Just a moment...

1007
00:39:25,041 --> 00:39:26,708
If Uncle finds out we came here,

1008
00:39:26,750 --> 00:39:27,541
he'll get angry!

1009
00:39:27,750 --> 00:39:29,166
Today he was arguing with Aqa Jan,

1010
00:39:29,208 --> 00:39:30,833
for renting the house to the Indians!

1011
00:39:31,375 --> 00:39:34,083
He thinks all Indians are British spies!

1012
00:39:34,416 --> 00:39:35,166
-Darling!

1013
00:39:35,208 --> 00:39:35,791
-Yeah, they are!

1014
00:39:35,833 --> 00:39:37,375
My friend! Asadollah!

1015
00:39:37,833 --> 00:39:38,833
Hello!

1016
00:39:38,875 --> 00:39:39,250
Hello to you!

1017
00:39:39,291 --> 00:39:43,208
Greetings to the great Sardar Maharat Khan!

1018
00:39:43,250 --> 00:39:43,791
Hello, Mr. Sardar.

1019
00:39:43,833 --> 00:39:45,208
Sardar! You went shopping yourself today!

1020
00:39:45,250 --> 00:39:47,791
We had migrant worker... did stealing... so we fire kartahe!

1021
00:39:47,791 --> 00:39:48,291
Shameless!

1022
00:39:48,333 --> 00:39:48,833
Please! Sit down!

1023
00:39:48,833 --> 00:39:49,416
Thank you, thank you!

1024
00:39:49,416 --> 00:39:50,500
Sit Saeed! Sit!

1025
00:39:52,625 --> 00:39:54,166
How come you kartahe remember us?

1026
00:39:54,208 --> 00:39:56,583
Indians attack our house kartahe,

1027
00:39:56,625 --> 00:39:58,125
We also attack Indian house!

1028
00:40:00,083 --> 00:40:01,875
You become very warlike, very intristing!

1029
00:40:01,875 --> 00:40:03,625
The world is very intristing!

1030
00:40:03,625 --> 00:40:04,916
You read newspaper?

1031
00:40:05,416 --> 00:40:06,500
Forget it!

1032
00:40:06,500 --> 00:40:07,166
Forget it?

1033
00:40:07,208 --> 00:40:08,625
What does "forget it" mean?

1034
00:40:08,750 --> 00:40:09,416
It means,

1035
00:40:10,208 --> 00:40:11,333
It means don't worry about it!

1036
00:40:12,625 --> 00:40:13,375
Let it go!

1037
00:40:14,083 --> 00:40:15,791
Now that everyone drinks blood,

1038
00:40:15,791 --> 00:40:17,375
we must... drink wine!

1039
00:40:18,291 --> 00:40:19,541
Long live! Long live!

1040
00:40:19,541 --> 00:40:21,541
(They laugh)

1041
00:40:22,875 --> 00:40:23,958
What did Asadollah say?

1042
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:24,833
- How are you, Saeed?

1043
00:40:24,833 --> 00:40:27,958
Indian attacked our country and we attacked them. - He's a good travel companion for San Francisco. Right?

1044
00:40:28,583 --> 00:40:30,333
Nowadays, everybody drinks blood.

1045
00:40:30,625 --> 00:40:32,041
Let's drink wine.

1046
00:40:32,708 --> 00:40:33,875
Long live! Long live!

1047
00:40:36,166 --> 00:40:37,708
Here! Would you have some wine?

1048
00:40:37,750 --> 00:40:38,375
No! I won't drink.

1049
00:40:38,375 --> 00:40:39,083
Saeed!

1050
00:40:39,291 --> 00:40:39,875
Drink wine!

1051
00:40:39,875 --> 00:40:40,708
Drink! - No, I won't drink!

1052
00:40:41,166 --> 00:40:41,958
Moment!

1053
00:40:42,666 --> 00:40:43,208
If you're a kid,

1054
00:40:43,250 --> 00:40:45,000
you've no right to fall in love!

1055
00:40:45,125 --> 00:40:46,083
If you're in love,

1056
00:40:46,125 --> 00:40:47,625
you've no right to refuse wine!

1057
00:40:47,833 --> 00:40:48,875
Take it from her!

1058
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:53,708
Remember, from the hand of a beautiful lady,

1059
00:40:54,083 --> 00:40:55,625
even if she gives you deadly poison,

1060
00:40:55,625 --> 00:40:56,416
don't refuse it!

1061
00:40:56,625 --> 00:40:57,333
Take it from her!

1062
00:40:57,791 --> 00:40:58,250
Thank you!

1063
00:40:58,375 --> 00:40:59,208
What did he say?

1064
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:00,500
He says

1065
00:41:00,750 --> 00:41:02,166
you should even take poison,

1066
00:41:02,375 --> 00:41:04,000
from a pretty young woman!

1067
00:41:04,041 --> 00:41:04,875
To your health! - To your health!

1068
00:41:04,916 --> 00:41:05,625
Good health!

1069
00:41:05,958 --> 00:41:06,625
To your health!

1070
00:41:10,041 --> 00:41:12,000
How come you kartahe remember us?

1071
00:41:12,416 --> 00:41:14,625
Today we want to kartahe spy game!

1072
00:41:15,250 --> 00:41:15,833
No! No!

1073
00:41:15,875 --> 00:41:17,000
I not do spying!

1074
00:41:17,250 --> 00:41:18,083
I not spy!

1075
00:41:18,083 --> 00:41:19,041
No! No! No!

1076
00:41:19,083 --> 00:41:19,583
No no!

1077
00:41:19,583 --> 00:41:20,416
Game!

1078
00:41:20,458 --> 00:41:21,500
Game, man!

1079
00:41:21,541 --> 00:41:22,791
Spy game!

1080
00:41:23,083 --> 00:41:23,625
Game!

1081
00:41:25,750 --> 00:41:26,708
Game!

1082
00:41:26,708 --> 00:41:28,333
Spy game!

1083
00:41:28,375 --> 00:41:28,875
What did he say?

1084
00:41:28,916 --> 00:41:31,875
As it says, we want to play spy game.

1085
00:41:31,916 --> 00:41:33,458
Oh, how nice!

1086
00:41:35,166 --> 00:41:37,166
How funny. What kind of a game is that?

1087
00:41:37,458 --> 00:41:38,125
Moment!

1088
00:41:38,416 --> 00:41:39,125
Moment!

1089
00:41:39,250 --> 00:41:41,291
This boy has an uncle,

1090
00:41:41,458 --> 00:41:42,666
like Napoleon!

1091
00:41:42,958 --> 00:41:44,041
Napoleon!

1092
00:41:44,166 --> 00:41:44,833
Yes, crazy!

1093
00:41:45,500 --> 00:41:45,875
Crazy?

1094
00:41:45,875 --> 00:41:46,625
Yes! Crazy!

1095
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:47,583
Madman!

1096
00:41:48,041 --> 00:41:49,750
He thought you are a spy!

1097
00:41:50,250 --> 00:41:51,500
We wanted to joke with him!

1098
00:41:51,666 --> 00:41:53,375
You must play spy game,

1099
00:41:53,416 --> 00:41:55,000
so we all kartahe laugh!

1100
00:41:55,083 --> 00:41:56,416
(They laugh)

1101
00:41:58,250 --> 00:41:59,708
Oh! Let's play...

1102
00:42:00,041 --> 00:42:01,083
Ok! Ok!

1103
00:42:01,458 --> 00:42:01,833
Cheers!

1104
00:42:01,875 --> 00:42:02,250
To your health!

1105
00:42:02,291 --> 00:42:03,083
To your health!

1106
00:42:03,125 --> 00:42:03,875
Happy drinking!

1107
00:42:03,916 --> 00:42:04,666
To your health! - To your health!

1108
00:42:04,666 --> 00:42:05,125
To your health!

1109
00:42:05,166 --> 00:42:06,750
Now what should we kartahe?

1110
00:42:08,833 --> 00:42:09,916
I teach you.

1111
00:42:10,458 --> 00:42:11,791
But must say in the ear!

1112
00:42:12,166 --> 00:42:13,250
Excuse me darling!

1113
00:42:13,375 --> 00:42:14,333
One moment! Please!

1114
00:42:14,416 --> 00:42:15,083
Where to?

1115
00:42:16,041 --> 00:42:18,375
Now that he thinks I am spy kartahe,

1116
00:42:18,375 --> 00:42:20,041
so I make joke with him!

1117
00:42:21,208 --> 00:42:22,375
He's heading to Qom.

1118
00:42:22,875 --> 00:42:23,833
For pilgrimage!

1119
00:42:24,083 --> 00:42:26,958
You must read a poem kartahe,

1120
00:42:27,083 --> 00:42:28,625
so Sir gets scared!

1121
00:42:28,666 --> 00:42:29,583
Of course that poem...

1122
00:42:29,583 --> 00:42:31,125
What are you whispering about?

1123
00:42:31,958 --> 00:42:32,458
Please!

1124
00:42:32,458 --> 00:42:34,333
It's about that game, darling.

1125
00:42:34,333 --> 00:42:35,000
Moment!

1126
00:42:35,000 --> 00:42:37,125
And Napoleon stay how many days in Qom kartahe?

1127
00:42:37,458 --> 00:42:38,833
Seven, eight, ten days.

1128
00:42:39,291 --> 00:42:43,000
How Napoleon endure separation and missing his wife kartahe?

1129
00:42:44,125 --> 00:42:46,083
His wife passed away kartahe.

1130
00:42:46,500 --> 00:42:47,583
For many years now,

1131
00:42:47,625 --> 00:42:50,250
Sir's nature is very much depressed!

1132
00:42:50,791 --> 00:42:51,583
So be it!

1133
00:42:51,583 --> 00:42:52,375
So be it!

1134
00:42:52,583 --> 00:42:54,750
Actually, I know one poem,

1135
00:42:54,791 --> 00:42:56,333
very suitable!

1136
00:42:57,416 --> 00:42:58,125
Bless you!

1137
00:42:58,166 --> 00:43:00,041
Very suitable for Nishapur!

1138
00:43:00,083 --> 00:43:01,083
Bless you, Sardar!

1139
00:43:01,125 --> 00:43:03,583
You really are so kind kartahe!

1140
00:43:03,625 --> 00:43:04,750
Bless you! You're the kind one!

1141
00:43:04,958 --> 00:43:05,875
Well...

1142
00:43:06,083 --> 00:43:07,500
You can rest easy now.

1143
00:43:07,541 --> 00:43:09,458
Now your uncle isn't going anywhere!

1144
00:43:09,750 --> 00:43:11,375
At least he's not going to Nishapur anymore!

1145
00:43:11,416 --> 00:43:13,083
Your Lily will stay with you, too.

1146
00:43:13,250 --> 00:43:14,000
Of course on the condition that,

1147
00:43:14,041 --> 00:43:16,166
you start thinking about San Francisco too! - Uncle Asdollah!

1148
00:43:16,250 --> 00:43:17,666
Don't say these things in front of them!

1149
00:43:17,833 --> 00:43:19,375
So why is your nature, so young,

1150
00:43:19,500 --> 00:43:21,208
also very much depressed!

1151
00:43:24,125 --> 00:43:25,416
I will sign the telegram,

1152
00:43:25,416 --> 00:43:28,625
in the name of Mr. Mortazavi!

1153
00:43:28,791 --> 00:43:31,250
I won't mention the children's names either.

1154
00:43:31,458 --> 00:43:33,000
When I send the telegram,

1155
00:43:33,000 --> 00:43:34,625
send the goods...

1156
00:43:34,916 --> 00:43:35,958
You should know,

1157
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:38,458
I mean Lily and Naneh Bolqeys.

1158
00:43:38,833 --> 00:43:40,416
Especially now,

1159
00:43:40,416 --> 00:43:43,041
I need your help more than ever.

1160
00:43:43,708 --> 00:43:45,833
Because I've decided,

1161
00:43:46,291 --> 00:43:48,458
to take Qasem with me too!

1162
00:43:48,750 --> 00:43:50,791
How come you suddenly changed your mind?

1163
00:43:53,291 --> 00:43:55,708
Qasem is from Qom.

1164
00:43:55,958 --> 00:43:59,000
I thought if I don't take him,

1165
00:43:59,458 --> 00:44:02,333
it might raise suspicion!

1166
00:44:03,333 --> 00:44:06,958
We must keep up appearances in such a way

1167
00:44:07,125 --> 00:44:09,750
that their spies don't get suspicious!

1168
00:44:10,500 --> 00:44:11,833
Do you follow?

1169
00:44:12,166 --> 00:44:14,708
Especially now, I need

1170
00:44:14,875 --> 00:44:16,083
your help more than ever.

1171
00:44:16,166 --> 00:44:18,958
Please instruct the driver,

1172
00:44:19,000 --> 00:44:21,791
because the road to Qom is very crowded these days,

1173
00:44:21,958 --> 00:44:23,958
to drive carefully. - Rest assured.

1174
00:44:23,958 --> 00:44:25,458
I am watching over everything.

1175
00:44:25,458 --> 00:44:26,083
Thank you.

1176
00:44:29,208 --> 00:44:32,291
I leave the home front to you.

1177
00:44:33,000 --> 00:44:34,291
In my absence,

1178
00:44:34,500 --> 00:44:36,375
You are my deputy.

1179
00:44:36,375 --> 00:44:36,958
Much obliged!

1180
00:44:39,250 --> 00:44:39,916
Khan brother!

1181
00:44:40,041 --> 00:44:40,833
Until we meet again.

1182
00:44:40,833 --> 00:44:43,291
God willing, you'll be back safe soon.

1183
00:44:45,458 --> 00:44:46,291
Everyone is upset.

1184
00:44:46,333 --> 00:44:48,083
But well, what can be done.

1185
00:44:49,291 --> 00:44:49,750
Brother!

1186
00:44:49,791 --> 00:44:52,166
Please take care of the children.

1187
00:44:53,000 --> 00:44:53,625
Safe travels!

1188
00:44:54,000 --> 00:44:56,208
Sir mustn't worry about a thing.

1189
00:44:59,083 --> 00:45:01,333
Sister, look after my house. - God willing, see you soon.

1190
00:45:01,333 --> 00:45:01,958
Yes!

1191
00:45:01,958 --> 00:45:03,208
No worries, Sir!

1192
00:45:03,250 --> 00:45:04,000
Safe travels.

1193
00:45:05,625 --> 00:45:07,833
He has no father or mother. They said that from the first day!

1194
00:45:07,833 --> 00:45:08,416
- Don't worry!

1195
00:45:08,458 --> 00:45:09,625
War and politics.

1196
00:45:09,708 --> 00:45:12,541
- Are two inseparable things.

1197
00:45:13,500 --> 00:45:15,250
- So where is Qasem?

1198
00:45:15,875 --> 00:45:18,208
- Where has he gone at this hour?

1199
00:45:20,791 --> 00:45:22,250
Sir, we beg you!

1200
00:45:22,291 --> 00:45:24,000
Please give up this trip!

1201
00:45:24,208 --> 00:45:25,291
Just now we went to the bazaar

1202
00:45:25,291 --> 00:45:26,750
to buy souvenirs,

1203
00:45:26,791 --> 00:45:28,000
They were saying the British army,

1204
00:45:28,041 --> 00:45:29,458
is just six miles from Qom!

1205
00:45:29,666 --> 00:45:31,375
They were saying they have cannons and guns,

1206
00:45:31,416 --> 00:45:33,166
that can blast from nine miles away!

1207
00:45:33,333 --> 00:45:36,541
Now you're trying to scare me with the British?

1208
00:45:37,791 --> 00:45:41,208
We don't complain of God's will,

1209
00:45:42,083 --> 00:45:45,416
a lion is not shamed by its chains!

1210
00:45:45,500 --> 00:45:47,208
Sir, you know us well!

1211
00:45:47,208 --> 00:45:48,875
We're not afraid of these things!

1212
00:45:48,916 --> 00:45:51,250
But why should we get ourselves into trouble for no reason!

1213
00:45:51,750 --> 00:45:53,041
Even Lady Masoumeh herself,

1214
00:45:53,083 --> 00:45:53,708
wouldn't be pleased,

1215
00:45:53,750 --> 00:45:55,666
for us to become prisoners of the British army!

1216
00:45:55,666 --> 00:45:56,750
If you're scared,

1217
00:45:56,791 --> 00:45:57,625
don't come!

1218
00:45:57,708 --> 00:45:59,166
Go hide in a corner of the basement

1219
00:45:59,208 --> 00:46:01,833
like old women!

1220
00:46:01,958 --> 00:46:03,750
We're not afraid of the British or their fathers!

1221
00:46:03,750 --> 00:46:04,541
Dad!

1222
00:46:05,500 --> 00:46:06,291
My dear dad.

1223
00:46:06,291 --> 00:46:07,916
Come, Mash Ghasem. Come, pass under the Quran.

1224
00:46:08,291 --> 00:46:10,041
Don't cry, my daughter.

1225
00:46:10,500 --> 00:46:11,916
It's nothing.

1226
00:46:12,708 --> 00:46:15,875
Uncle Colonel will take care of you,

1227
00:46:15,916 --> 00:46:18,375
until I return from the pilgrimage.

1228
00:46:18,375 --> 00:46:19,083
Brother!

1229
00:46:19,375 --> 00:46:20,291
I'm entrusting Lily

1230
00:46:20,333 --> 00:46:21,750
to your hands. - Come, my daughter.

1231
00:46:21,750 --> 00:46:22,333
- Come

1232
00:46:22,333 --> 00:46:23,583
Don't cry, my dear.

1233
00:46:23,583 --> 00:46:24,375
Go.

1234
00:46:24,416 --> 00:46:25,333
Don't cry.

1235
00:46:26,125 --> 00:46:28,083
It's nothing, why are you crying, my dear?

1236
00:46:28,125 --> 00:46:28,958
Don't cry-

1237
00:46:29,000 --> 00:46:30,583
- They'll go and come back safely, God willing.

1238
00:46:30,583 --> 00:46:31,500
- Calm down, my dear.

1239
00:46:34,541 --> 00:46:35,750
God be with you.

1240
00:46:36,583 --> 00:46:37,916
Why are you crying, calm down!

1241
00:46:40,291 --> 00:46:42,541
May God protect you, Khan brother.

1242
00:46:42,666 --> 00:46:43,291
Safe travels.

1243
00:46:43,541 --> 00:46:44,833
- Come back soon. - Safe travels, Khan brother.

1244
00:46:45,333 --> 00:46:46,166
Godspeed.

1245
00:46:46,208 --> 00:46:48,041
May God keep you safe, Khan brother.

1246
00:46:49,125 --> 00:46:49,791
Lily!

1247
00:46:49,833 --> 00:46:51,250
Don't cry so much! - Goodbye.

1248
00:46:51,708 --> 00:46:54,208
It's bad luck to cry as a traveler leaves.

1249
00:46:55,166 --> 00:46:57,375
(Crowd murmur)

1250
00:46:57,541 --> 00:46:58,250
Qasem!

1251
00:46:58,625 --> 00:46:59,583
Did you bring the rifle?

1252
00:46:59,625 --> 00:47:00,291
Yes, Sir.

1253
00:47:01,666 --> 00:47:02,291
Sir!

1254
00:47:02,666 --> 00:47:05,208
Mr. Seyyed Abolghasem has arrived.

1255
00:47:05,333 --> 00:47:07,250
May God protect you, God willing!

1256
00:47:07,250 --> 00:47:08,041
Let me kiss your hand!

1257
00:47:08,083 --> 00:47:08,583
Thank you!

1258
00:47:08,583 --> 00:47:09,083
- He's here!

1259
00:47:09,083 --> 00:47:10,791
I hope you are well, sir?

1260
00:47:10,791 --> 00:47:11,458
- Thanks to your kindness.

1261
00:47:11,458 --> 00:47:12,208
Are you in good health?

1262
00:47:12,541 --> 00:47:13,583
Thank you! Thank you!

1263
00:47:13,625 --> 00:47:16,375
We heard you intend to visit the shrine of Lady Masoumeh!

1264
00:47:16,583 --> 00:47:18,000
We were feeling down,

1265
00:47:18,041 --> 00:47:21,125
so we thought we'd go pay our respects for a few days.

1266
00:47:21,166 --> 00:47:22,083
God willing, all will be well!

1267
00:47:22,125 --> 00:47:23,125
May it be blessed, God willing!

1268
00:47:23,166 --> 00:47:25,666
Ah! Seyyed Abolghasem! His Eminence Hojjat al-Islam!

1269
00:47:25,708 --> 00:47:26,875
How is the young master?

1270
00:47:26,916 --> 00:47:27,416
Thanks to your kindness.

1271
00:47:27,416 --> 00:47:28,833
In the next few days, God willing, we plan

1272
00:47:28,875 --> 00:47:30,958
to get him engaged to a good girl.

1273
00:47:31,250 --> 00:47:32,916
The daughter of Haj Ali Khan, the master architect.

1274
00:47:33,625 --> 00:47:34,208
Ha! The master architect!

1275
00:47:34,250 --> 00:47:36,291
Bravo! Well done!

1276
00:47:36,291 --> 00:47:37,208
Well done!

1277
00:47:37,250 --> 00:47:40,583
She is a very respectable and sensible girl, Sir!

1278
00:47:40,625 --> 00:47:43,166
Please visit us from time to time.

1279
00:47:43,291 --> 00:47:45,625
(Everyone laughs)

1280
00:47:46,291 --> 00:47:47,000
- My dear dad.

1281
00:47:48,083 --> 00:47:50,458
I leave you all to God, sister.

1282
00:47:50,500 --> 00:47:52,416
May God protect you, Khan brother. - Safe travels.

1283
00:47:52,416 --> 00:47:55,458
- Goodbye. - Safe travels, Sir, safe travels.

1284
00:47:55,500 --> 00:47:57,416
(Crowd murmur)

1285
00:47:58,291 --> 00:47:59,875
- Safe journey. - Goodbye.

1286
00:48:00,375 --> 00:48:01,083
- Safe travels.

1287
00:48:01,333 --> 00:48:03,166
(Crowd murmur)

1288
00:48:04,250 --> 00:48:05,416
- Godspeed.

1289
00:48:06,083 --> 00:48:07,500
Goodbye, goodbye...

1290
00:48:07,541 --> 00:48:09,333
- May God protect you, Sir.

1291
00:48:09,375 --> 00:48:10,291
- Safe journey.

1292
00:48:10,291 --> 00:48:11,000
- Goodbye.

1293
00:48:11,625 --> 00:48:12,833
It's nothing, Lily dear!

1294
00:48:12,833 --> 00:48:14,458
Don't cry so much, my dear! Don't cry!

1295
00:48:14,500 --> 00:48:15,041
- Don't cry.

1296
00:48:15,375 --> 00:48:16,875
- Don't cry as they leave. It's bad luck.

1297
00:48:16,916 --> 00:48:17,750
- Let's go to the door.

1298
00:48:18,333 --> 00:48:19,416
Safe travels!

1299
00:48:26,291 --> 00:48:28,625
(Sound of children playing)

1300
00:48:32,625 --> 00:48:33,541
Stop!

1301
00:48:36,291 --> 00:48:37,208
Sir!

1302
00:48:42,333 --> 00:48:43,750
Sir! He's coming toward us!

1303
00:48:43,958 --> 00:48:45,000
Oh, good Lord!

1304
00:48:45,625 --> 00:48:46,958
Have a pleasant journey, sir!

1305
00:48:47,541 --> 00:48:49,791
We all kartahe miss you!

1306
00:48:49,791 --> 00:48:50,750
Thank you very much!

1307
00:48:50,916 --> 00:48:53,250
How good that we saw you so we could

1308
00:48:53,291 --> 00:48:54,291
say goodbye!

1309
00:48:54,541 --> 00:48:56,791
It's been a while since we've been

1310
00:48:56,916 --> 00:48:59,000
to Lady Masoumeh's shrine!

1311
00:48:59,041 --> 00:49:00,208
But weren't you afraid at all,

1312
00:49:00,250 --> 00:49:02,666
that the road might be unsafe? With this war and conflict?

1313
00:49:02,666 --> 00:49:03,291
Sir?

1314
00:49:03,583 --> 00:49:05,166
No, no Sardar!

1315
00:49:05,208 --> 00:49:07,416
These are all just rumors!

1316
00:49:07,458 --> 00:49:09,833
What does the war have to do with us?

1317
00:49:09,875 --> 00:49:10,250
- Yes!

1318
00:49:10,250 --> 00:49:12,375
Besides, God forbid, if anything happens,

1319
00:49:12,416 --> 00:49:14,583
Lady Masoumeh herself protects the pilgrims!

1320
00:49:14,625 --> 00:49:16,958
- Yes!

1321
00:49:16,958 --> 00:49:17,333
Sir!

1322
00:49:17,375 --> 00:49:17,750
Sir!

1323
00:49:17,791 --> 00:49:20,750
Why didn't you kartahe take your child and family with you?

1324
00:49:21,291 --> 00:49:22,041
A few days!

1325
00:49:22,083 --> 00:49:24,500
It won't take more than a few days!

1326
00:49:24,500 --> 00:49:25,875
Yes! A few days...

1327
00:49:26,041 --> 00:49:26,708
Yes.

1328
00:49:26,750 --> 00:49:27,708
But sir!

1329
00:49:27,833 --> 00:49:30,291
Separation, no matter how short,

1330
00:49:30,333 --> 00:49:32,458
is still very heart-wrenching...

1331
00:49:33,083 --> 00:49:34,500
As the poet says:

1332
00:49:34,916 --> 00:49:38,916
My beloved is in Lahavard and I am in Nishapur...

1333
00:49:38,958 --> 00:49:40,166
M... m... m... Mohammad Aqa!

1334
00:49:40,250 --> 00:49:41,125
Let's go!

1335
00:49:41,416 --> 00:49:42,750
Qasem, don't look at him!

1336
00:49:44,500 --> 00:49:45,291
- Safe travels.

1337
00:49:45,791 --> 00:49:47,125
Uncle! Don't forget the souvenirs.

1338
00:49:47,166 --> 00:49:48,375
- My dear dad, God protect you! - Lily dear, take care!

1339
00:49:48,666 --> 00:49:49,208
- Goodbye.

1340
00:49:49,208 --> 00:49:49,541
- Get out of the way!

1341
00:49:49,541 --> 00:49:50,166
- Goodbye.

1342
00:49:50,291 --> 00:49:51,333
- Godspeed. - Safe travels.

1343
00:49:51,541 --> 00:49:52,375
- May God be with you.

1344
00:49:52,375 --> 00:49:53,125
- Goodbye!

1345
00:49:53,166 --> 00:49:54,208
- Goodbye.

1346
00:49:54,208 --> 00:49:55,041
- Goodbye.

1347
00:49:55,208 --> 00:49:56,125
- Safe travels.

1348
00:49:56,250 --> 00:49:58,916
(Crowd murmur)

1349
00:50:03,666 --> 00:50:05,625
Now go to your love with peace of mind!

1350
00:50:05,666 --> 00:50:06,166
Prince!

1351
00:50:06,333 --> 00:50:07,208
Yes, my dear?

1352
00:50:07,250 --> 00:50:10,375
Tonight I've made Aash Reshteh for Sir's safe journey.

1353
00:50:10,416 --> 00:50:11,208
Don't forget to come!

1354
00:50:11,250 --> 00:50:11,916
Sardar!

1355
00:50:11,958 --> 00:50:13,750
Tonight at Sir's house, I cooked Aash Reshteh!

1356
00:50:13,875 --> 00:50:15,625
You and the lady should also come.

1357
00:50:15,666 --> 00:50:16,458
No! No! No!

1358
00:50:16,500 --> 00:50:18,083
We don't want to trouble you.

1359
00:50:18,125 --> 00:50:19,250
There will be plenty of other opportunities

1360
00:50:19,291 --> 00:50:21,000
One day, God willing, another day!

1361
00:50:21,541 --> 00:50:22,333
Moment!

1362
00:50:22,375 --> 00:50:23,708
Sardar, no trouble at all!

1363
00:50:23,750 --> 00:50:25,750
By your life, the lady is kartahe upset!

1364
00:50:25,791 --> 00:50:26,833
You won't be upset, madam?

1365
00:50:27,500 --> 00:50:28,125
Well...

1366
00:50:28,166 --> 00:50:30,375
Please come, you'd be most welcome!

1367
00:50:30,416 --> 00:50:31,666
What are you saying, woman!

1368
00:50:32,125 --> 00:50:34,000
This Indian is coming to Khan brother's house tonight?

1369
00:50:34,375 --> 00:50:35,166
How strange!

1370
00:50:35,208 --> 00:50:36,666
This Asdollah has lost his mind!

1371
00:50:36,916 --> 00:50:38,166
Bravo, Sardar!

1372
00:50:38,208 --> 00:50:39,583
You recited a very excellent poem!

1373
00:50:40,250 --> 00:50:41,041
Thank you!

1374
00:50:41,166 --> 00:50:41,875
Hello!

1375
00:50:41,916 --> 00:50:45,000
Oh! My lady! Lady Maharat Khan!

1376
00:50:45,458 --> 00:50:47,250
My dear! How are you?

1377
00:50:48,041 --> 00:50:50,041
Fine! Thank you! And how are you?

1378
00:50:50,708 --> 00:50:51,333
Fine!

1379
00:50:52,000 --> 00:50:53,541
Tonight! You are our guest!

1380
00:50:53,625 --> 00:50:55,208
Aash reshteh with laugh!

1381
00:50:55,708 --> 00:50:56,291
Ok!

1382
00:50:56,666 --> 00:50:57,750
Oh, definitely!

1383
00:50:57,916 --> 00:50:59,916
If Sardar has no other engagements.

1384
00:51:00,416 --> 00:51:01,000
Sardar!

1385
00:51:01,000 --> 00:51:02,250
The lady agrees!

1386
00:51:02,750 --> 00:51:05,166
You have done a kindness kartahe,

1387
00:51:05,208 --> 00:51:06,833
You are most welcome.

1388
00:51:07,041 --> 00:51:09,416
Tonight we will laugh a lot kartahe!

1389
00:51:09,458 --> 00:51:10,708
If the lady agrees,

1390
00:51:10,708 --> 00:51:11,625
we also agree!

1391
00:51:11,666 --> 00:51:12,416
Goodbye!

1392
00:51:12,458 --> 00:51:12,833
Yes!

1393
00:51:12,875 --> 00:51:13,500
Don't be late!

1394
00:51:19,833 --> 00:51:21,666
You ate her up with your eyes!

1395
00:51:23,333 --> 00:51:24,833
Oh, damn you!

1396
00:51:25,208 --> 00:51:25,958
Hello!

1397
00:51:26,416 --> 00:51:27,166
Bye bye!

1398
00:51:29,166 --> 00:51:29,875
My dear!

1399
00:51:30,625 --> 00:51:32,250
Tonight, keep your eyes to yourself!

1400
00:51:32,291 --> 00:51:33,208
Why?

1401
00:51:34,083 --> 00:51:36,500
This Sardar has two cobras in his house,

1402
00:51:36,500 --> 00:51:37,625
kept in a cage!

1403
00:51:38,208 --> 00:51:39,958
Whoever looks lustfully at his wife,

1404
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:40,833
at night he takes one of the snakes,

1405
00:51:40,833 --> 00:51:42,541
and throws it in his bed!

1406
00:51:43,541 --> 00:51:44,791
Really? - Yes!

1407
00:51:45,166 --> 00:51:46,458
I swear to God!

1408
00:51:47,041 --> 00:51:48,458
Don't think I'm joking!

1409
00:51:48,500 --> 00:51:49,833
Do you want me to take you right now and show you!

1410
00:51:49,916 --> 00:51:51,208
Are you serious, Asdollah?

1411
00:51:51,625 --> 00:51:52,833
I swear!

1412
00:51:52,875 --> 00:51:54,541
No one knows they keep snakes in their house!

1413
00:51:54,541 --> 00:51:55,750
No one!

1414
00:51:56,208 --> 00:51:58,333
Lady Maharat Khan herself told me!

1415
00:51:58,750 --> 00:52:00,208
Tonight don't mention Lady Maharat Khan's name

1416
00:52:00,250 --> 00:52:01,708
in front of Aziz, for God's sake!

1417
00:52:01,958 --> 00:52:04,041
Otherwise from tomorrow we'll have trouble with Aziz!

1418
00:52:04,083 --> 00:52:05,000
He thinks that,

1419
00:52:05,041 --> 00:52:06,708
I fell in love with the English woman!

1420
00:52:07,000 --> 00:52:08,791
That other time it was also because of your jokes,

1421
00:52:08,833 --> 00:52:11,083
that she came to bed with the kitchen knife!

1422
00:52:11,125 --> 00:52:12,708
Moment!

1423
00:52:15,125 --> 00:52:18,333
♪ Ride of the valkyrie ♪

